	file.0000000000000001.title: "WinterCraft-Eternal Winter"
	quest.006785C0F6AD7505.quest_desc: [
		"What is it?"
		""
		"Rechiseled adds over 600+ decorative variants for vanilla blocks. It’s the ultimate tool for anyone who wants connected textures and better-looking builds!"
		""
		"The Chisel"
		"Right-Click: Opens the UI to pick your favorite variant."
		"Left-Click: Changes blocks already placed in the world."
		""
		"The Menu"
		"Put a block inside to see all its versions. You can also swap between full blocks, stairs, and slabs, or toggle connected textures on and off."
		""
		"In-World Editing"
		"Left-click any placed block to cycle its look. If you have a block stored in the chisel, it’ll transform whatever you click into that specific style."
	]
	quest.01C0DC225CB25A0C.quest_subtitle: "Hunter addon allows the laser to target mobs"
	quest.01C0DC225CB25A0C.title: "Hurting Mobs"
	quest.01C9AA8FE582A46A.quest_desc: [
		"A quarter of a hundred. Impressive."
		""
		"At this point, you've probably memorized the respawn screen better than your own base. The eternal winter has claimed you twenty-five times, and yet here you are, still standing. Or lying dead again. Details."
		""
		"The pack was tested. It was beaten. The developer didn't die this many times. Just saying."
		""
		"But hey, persistence is a skill too. Maybe not the one you wanted, but it's the one you have."
		""
		"Keep going. The snow doesn't care about your feelings."
	]
	quest.01C9AA8FE582A46A.quest_subtitle: "come back when you die this many times"
	quest.01C9AA8FE582A46A.title: "25"
	quest.02315D55EB638E3C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.02315D55EB638E3C.quest_subtitle: "Make biomass to use it"
	quest.03686BD4D587CA49.quest_desc: ["each fully broken limb will reduce your maximum health. However, you won’t die outright if your head or entire body is fully broken but it will severely impact your chances of survival, bringing you closer to certain death."]
	quest.038B0EDEBCC4DC01.quest_desc: [
		"How to find water in places where there is none? Well... in this modpack, that’s not exactly \"essential\" knowledge. However, you can find Water Plants that will help you access purified water in the desert."
		""
		"Though, I’m not sure if you’ll even see them under all that snow... "
		""
		"Check the image above for some information that (probably) won't be useful to you. Unless... maybe in the Nether?"
	]
	quest.040C925FE89A4C02.quest_desc: [
		"Cryptic Eye - Have a small chance to get it when enchanting"
		""
		"No information about this eye"
	]
	quest.048DA51510867EF5.quest_desc: [
		"Cursed Eye - Found in Bastions treasure chest"
		""
		" A powerful yet destructive artifact; the Piglins swore to protect it at the cost of their lives"
	]
	quest.050DC78BA933062A.quest_desc: [
		"Functions like a normal anvil, but with the following changes:"
		"Never breaks"
		"No level cap"
		"The required level cost will not exceed 30"
	]
	quest.05ABFD52E776C99D.quest_desc: [
		"In this eternal winter, your pockets are never deep enough. It's time to craft a Backpack!"
		""
		"Press 'B' to open the Backpack Menu. Here, you can equip or swap your backpacks."
		""
		"Your backpack starts small. Use your Experience (XP) or Unlock Tokens directly in the menu to purchase more storage slots."
		""
		"Want to carry more? Spend XP to increase the number of backpacks you can wear at once!"
		""
		"Augments: Unlock special upgrades (Augments) with XP to give your backpack unique abilities."
		"Style and Identity: You can rename your backpack or unlock new visual styles to look like a true winter explorer.\""
	]
	quest.05B187C517924B29.quest_desc: [
		"Create has a very unique way of storing items and doing autocrafting. "
		"Item Vaults can store a large amount of items but they do not have a standard interface to see what is inside. "
		""
		"You can use Packagers to wrap items up and ship them to other storages to create an inventory sorting system. Stock Links help connect items in a storage to your storage network. When you combine this with a Stock Ticker you can request items from all those linked storages."
	]
	quest.05B187C517924B29.title: "Create's Inventory?"
	quest.05CB09C7C79EFF2E.quest_desc: [
		"The most basic item to heal your limbs is the Healing Herbs, you can eat it and click on the limb you wish to heal. "
		""
		"There are other healing items that allow to heal multiple limbs at once or even heal your entire body while regenerating some of your hearts."
		""
		""
		"There are a total of 6 Healing Items, even though these can heal one or more limbs it doesnt mean that it will heal them fully, you might need to consume multiple healin herbs or maybe just use one or two bandages."
	]
	quest.06B2E71E4D531264.quest_desc: [
		"Warming Coats will grant you resistance to Cold, making it easier to witstand the coldness."
		""
		"Common Warming Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Cold Resistance by 2.0"
		""
		"Rare Warming Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Cold Resistance by 3.0"
		""
		"Epic Warming Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Cold Resistance by 4.0"
	]
	quest.0730BB030E852017.quest_desc: [
		"Rogue Eye - Found in Jungle Pyramids"
		""
		"This eye is believed to have given our ancestors the knowledge of Redstone"
	]
	quest.0789F03965EC1BB7.quest_desc: [
		"What's a hunter without a trophy room? The Taxidermy Table lets you turn those animal heads into epic wall decorations."
		"Just place a head on the table, wheet and mount and craft it into a Trophy. It’s the perfect way to make your base look like a true survivalist's cabin!"
	]
	quest.078FA175DB86C919.quest_desc: [
		"Creates permanent Portal connection"
		""
		"Can be connected with Portal spell"
	]
	quest.0815C76490828972.quest_desc: [
		"You got power? Cool. Now you need to actually move it somewhere."
		""
		"That's where Energy Pipes come in. Slap these down and run them from your generators to whatever needs juice. Simple as that."
		""
		"No magic, no weird rules. Just pipes carrying energy from point A to point B. You'll be using these a lot, so get comfortable with them."
	]
	quest.0815C76490828972.title: "Energy Pipe"
	quest.0841EB4541C83A23.quest_desc: ["The Water Purifier allows you to safely drink dirty water."]
	quest.087C30F0EFA284FB.quest_desc: [
		"A late game item crafted with echo shards and phantom membrane"
		"Serves as a temporary bed that does not set your spawn point"
		"When used will immediately place the player in sleep mode on the spot"
		"Upon waking up they will go back in your inventory. Perfect for camping!"
		"Does not prevent Phantom spawn nor provide any benefit"
	]
	quest.088040F2695ECF4E.quest_desc: [
		"Want to level up your food game? The Meat Grinder is where the magic happens."
		"You can turn beef or lamb into minced meat, or go full chef and make sausages (you’ll need intestines and an attachment for that!). If you’ve got leftovers like heads or spare carcasses, just grind them into scrap meat. Waste not, want not!"
	]
	quest.09342029BD641992.quest_desc: ["A dyeable bobber that can be dyed like leather armor. Doesn't work on vanilla rod."]
	quest.093EF22C53B957E2.quest_desc: [
		"Don’t throw away the \"trash\" from your butchery! The Pestle and Mortar is your best friend for recycling."
		"You can grind wishbones into bonemeal, hooves into slimeballs, and even special bones into their respective meals. It’s all about efficiency in the tundra!"
	]
	quest.09FB8AC7571E0E2E.quest_desc: ["deal extra damage underwater."]
	quest.0AB8869C30F661A1.quest_desc: [
		"3 Body Limbs"
		""
		"Regenerates 3.0 Health over 15.0s"
	]
	quest.0AD08E11451B88CE.quest_desc: [
		"To automate the water, you can craft a Water Pump over a water source next to water separator."
		""
		"The Water Pump need to be powered!"
	]
	quest.0ADAA5227D587196.quest_desc: ["Above, you can see all the modifiers that affect your body temperature. It’s definitely worth a look if you’re not sure what's making you freeze or overheat."]
	quest.0ADAA5227D587196.title: "Temperature Modifiers"
	quest.0C9F9196CA49FF8D.quest_desc: ["Find nickel, copper and steel ore to find begin your journey"]
	quest.0C9F9196CA49FF8D.title: "Oritech Beginnings"
	quest.0CE78ABFB8A11BE8.quest_desc: ["Place your backpack in this dock to access your items without wearing it. It is a great way to manage your storage while staying inside your base."]
	quest.0CF69DBA9573A7B3.quest_desc: [
		"The Schematic Table is basically your copy/paste tool for buildings. It reads structures from a schematic file and writes them into the world for you."
		""
		"Super handy if you wanna duplicate your base, or if you found a cool design online and just want to plop it down without doing all the block placing yourself. Great for sharing builds with friends too."
	]
	quest.0D5079233573A022.quest_desc: ["Causes fish to escape slower when you aren't reeling them in"]
	quest.0D9B001405689765.quest_desc: [
		"Drawer Controllers are the special block. They will search for any connected drawer within 50 blocks by default (configurable), and then expose all of those drawers as a large combined inventory. This lets you hook up a single pipe, tube, duct, spark, storage bus, etc. and interact with the entire bank of drawers."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The second function of the controller is as a deposit-only interactive block. By right-clicking on the front face with an item, the item will be deposited into the connected network. By double-right clicking, it will attempt to dump your entire inventory. Items will only be dumped if they already exist in the network, allowing you to clear out a bunch of mob drops or farmed crops without literally dumping your entire inventory."
	]
	quest.0E61A89C2E992B2E.quest_desc: ["Use the freezer to turn water buckets into ice and chill your stuff"]
	quest.0EC0F93FA4B4BE49.quest_desc: ["This machine can only be powered by &5Enderic Lasers&r. Used to craft high value items."]
	quest.0EC0F93FA4B4BE49.quest_subtitle: "Ultimate crafting machine"
	quest.0EF59DD53D92768C.quest_desc: [
		"Food and drinks can be your best defense against the weather. Some items provide special effects that will either increase or decrease your body temperature."
		""
		"There are multiple options to help you fight the extreme conditions. For the best results, you can stack effects: combine hot food with a hot drink to warm up faster, or cold food with a cold drink to cool down."
		""
		"Check the image below for more details!"
	]
	quest.0EF5CDA028DE89AB.quest_desc: ["[ { \"text\": \"Electric Boiler?\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"79E8A53149824928\" } } ]"]
	quest.0F16498769DFB3B0.quest_desc: ["What will we need all that &8Andesite&r for? We'll need &8Andesite Alloys&r! \\n\\n&8Andesite Alloys&r are made by combining 2 &8Andesite&r with either 2 &7Iron Nuggets&r or 2 &7Zinc Nuggets&r. \\n\\n&8Andesite Alloys&r don't do much on their own, rather they are the Crafting Ingrediant for almost all Machines and Items. So yeah, we'll need a few."]
	quest.0F16498769DFB3B0.title: "&8Andesite Alloys"
	quest.0F36BD45DC943612.quest_desc: [
		"Quality Equipment! Every tool, piece of armor, or Bauble has a chance to receive a Quality, which can either strengthen or weaken your item. All Quality names have been specially adapted to match the atmosphere of this pack."
		""
		"To reforge your tools, you will need a Reforging Station, in which you will combine equipment with its repair item. If a repair item does not exist for the equipment, it will use the default material."
	]
	quest.0F36BD45DC943612.title: "Quality Equipment "
	quest.0F9E0EE4517479F3.quest_desc: [
		"While you can just slap a bobber on a basic rod, the Tackle Box is where the real pro-fishing happens. It’s like a specialized workbench and backpack for your fishing obsession."
		""
		"What you need to know:"
		""
		"Ditch the Vanilla Rod: Heads up! You cannot use the standard Vanilla rod here. To unlock the full potential of the Tackle Box, you need a rod from Aquaculture 2 (like the Iron or Gold ones)."
		""
		"Full Customization: Only with a modded rod and the Tackle Box can you equip Fishing Lines, Hooks, and Bait. These are game-changers that make catching rare fish way easier."
		""
		"Organization: It’s a dedicated storage for all your gear. No more cluttering your inventory with hooks and slimy bait."
		""
		"Easy Access: Just place it down, pop your modded rod inside, and customize it to fit your needs."
		"Quick Tip: Get a modded rod ASAP if you want to use anything more than just a simple bobber. It's the only way to reach those deep-sea treasures!"
	]
	quest.0FD0DB134F9E1517.quest_desc: ["Dropped from hoglins"]
	quest.0FFB3DCF5815B287.quest_desc: [
		"Juices are the superior way to stay hydrated. Unlike plain water, several juices provide both normal hydration and saturation, which essentially acts like a double hydration bar."
		""
		"This makes them much more efficient for long journeys in the cold. Check the image above to see how the bars look when you're well-nourished!"
	]
	quest.105394CCD2226940.quest_desc: [
		"Have you noticed yet? The sky is no longer part of this world."
		"It has become its judge."
		""
		"Villagers are bound to the world's order—and the sky has rejected them. Animals live outside its law. But the Player... the Player belongs to neither."
		""
		"What does this mean? From now on, Villagers will perish when exposed to the open sky. But that is only the beginning of their struggle. What else has changed?"
		"You will have to find out for yourself..."
	]
	quest.105394CCD2226940.title: "Villagers"
	quest.114EACA9B32B32FB.quest_subtitle: "You know the deal..."
	quest.11807FB11785B010.quest_desc: [
		"Head (Headache): Causes sudden blindness every now and then. Absolute nightmare in combat."
		""
		"Torso (Vulnerability): You’re \"paper-thin.\" Every hit (except falling) hurts 20% more."
		""
		"Leg (Hard Falling): Falls hurt 20% more. Watch your step and where you jump."
		""
		"Foot (Slowness): Forget about sprinting. Slows you down by 15%."
		""
		"Arm (Mining Fatigue): Mining and attacking are 10% slower. It’s a real drag."
	]
	quest.11877BF470E271C2.quest_desc: [
		"1 Body Limbs"
		""
		"Regenerates 3.0 Health over 20.0s"
	]
	quest.11879EDFC34C120F.quest_desc: ["Shows what fish is on your line before it's caught!"]
	quest.11A4C57600E692EC.quest_subtitle: "Increase energy capacity of machine"
	quest.11AB59E17E25B7B4.quest_desc: [
		"Want to make a fresh Pizza or some crunchy Toast? I know I do! But your old campfire won't cut it for these gourmet treats. It’s time to modernize your kitchen."
		""
		"To get started, you'll need an Electric Stove and a Toaster. "
		""
		"These aren't magic—they need power. Your first step is building a Coal Generator to get some juice flowing. Grab some coal and let’s plug it in!"
	]
	quest.11AB59E17E25B7B4.title: "Generator"
	quest.12274935C3D20C74.quest_desc: ["Like the entirity of Building Tips in &6&lATM10&r, I can't teach you how to design your &5Train&r... but I can give Tips! \\n\\nThere is tons of different Building Blocks you can use, lots of the &6&lCreate&r Casings look clean and Concretes can help give a more slick look. \\n\\nYou can also use Doors and Trapdoors within the &5Train&r which can also be used when the &5Train&r is moving. \\n\\nWhat about making it look pretty? Well Stairs, Slabs, and Trapdoors help give Shape to it as well as the Flywheel or &dCogs&r give nice round edges. \\n\\nHeck you can even put a Campfire on it to make a Steam Engine!"]
	quest.12274935C3D20C74.title: "Decorating your &5Train&r"
	quest.124CD4B8876B81F6.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.124CD4B8876B81F6.quest_subtitle: "Store the power you generate"
	quest.124CD4B8876B81F6.title: "Storing Energy"
	quest.127F9EAC7C305BF5.quest_desc: [
		"The Wrench is basically the Swiss Army knife of Create. Rotate blocks, pop them off instantly, tweak settings—what doesn't this thing do?"
		""
		"To break any Create block, just Shift + Right Click. Done. No mining required."
		""
		"To rotate something, just a normal Right Click with the Wrench. Sadly it doesn't give us free Rotational Power, but hey, at least it fixes your placement screw-ups."
		""
		"It'll also come in clutch later when you start messing with Contraptions. But we'll get to that."
	]
	quest.127F9EAC7C305BF5.title: "Wrench"
	quest.131381A6670D6F38.quest_desc: [
		"The Vacuumator allow you to put food inside Cans that you can eat in space."
		""
		"For this machine to work you need to put a can in the first slot, food in the second and an empty glass bottle in the third. The machine will give you a can with food inside and a water bottle."
	]
	quest.133CA315A1443A49.quest_desc: ["&bMechanical Pumps&r will use Rotational Power to move &bFluids&r through &bPipes&r. \\n\\nFirst, replace a &bPipe&r with the &bMechanical Pump&r. Then, make sure it is facing the right way you want &bFluids&r to be moved. The Arrows next to the internal &6Cog&r will tell which direction it will move, you can change that with a Wrench. \\n\\nThen, feed it &dRotational Power&r with a &6Cog&r near it. The direction does not change anything, but the Speed will effect how quickly &bFluids&r are moved. \\n\\n&bMechanical Pumps&r will also be needed for other Machines like the &bHose Pulley&r!"]
	quest.133CA315A1443A49.title: "&bMechanical Pump"
	quest.13AEBC331F29BC3D.quest_desc: ["&eItem Logistics&r is important to &6&lCreate&r. &6Millstones&r need &eItems&f, &6Deployers &fneed &eItems&f, &6Mechanical Mixers&f need &eItems&r, and so on. \\n\\nNow how does &6&lCreate&r want us to move &eItems&r? With &eBelts&r! \\n\\n&eBelts&r can be attached to two &8Shafts&r to connect and move with them. If the first &8Shaft&r is moving &e&oClockwise&r, the second will move same Speed and Direction. \\n\\nSame with the &eBelts&r that are placed on those &8Shafts&r, they will move same Speed and Direction as the &8Shafts&r they are placed between. \\n\\nWith placing &8Belts&r they can be placed perfectly Horizontal, Vertical, or diagonal at 45% angles. \\n\\nOnce placed and move, any &eItems&r or Entities will be moved with the &eBelt&r. Entities can walk off the &eBelts&r though so careful with that. Thankfully &eItems&r can't walk off or even despawn when on it! \\n\\nThe &eItems&r will then be taken to wherever the &eBelt&r goes. If it abruptly ends, the &eItems&r will just be Dropped. If it goes to a &eDepot&r, the &eItem&r will be placed in a &eDepot&r. If it goes below a &6Machine&r, the&6 Machine&r will use it. \\n\\nIf you want to take &eItems &foff the &eBelt&r you can just Right Click it!"]
	quest.13AEBC331F29BC3D.title: "&e&lItem Logistics"
	quest.13B9E37EB255BB24.quest_desc: [
		"Alright, you've got iron. Now you're probably wondering how to actually get around this cursed world."
		""
		"Tons of options, my friend. Classic Minecraft stuff: rails and minecarts, boats—underground water highways are underrated by the way—horses, llamas, whatever floats your boat. Literally."
		""
		"Elytra? Yeah, that's endgame. We'll get there."
		""
		"But you can also use magic or tech. Build a whole train with Create if you're feeling fancy. How? Like a 10 minute YouTube tutorial and you're set. It's not quantum engineering, you'll manage."
		""
		"Pick your ride and stop walking everywhere like a peasant."
	]
	quest.14DF6537559086BF.quest_desc: [
		"Sun Fern. You can find these scattered across the world. They are an essential ingredient for crafting Warm String and Heat Resistance potions."
		"Good luck finding them buried under all that snow."
	]
	quest.14DF6537559086BF.quest_subtitle: "Ocieplenie"
	quest.14E2DC584D627ACF.title: "Hammocks"
	quest.152C3934F9F202BF.quest_desc: [
		"Before We Dive In"
		""
		"Quick heads up. I'm not gonna sit here and explain every little thing about Create or Oritech. You've seen these mods before. Create is in like every pack, and Oritech isn't exactly new either."
		""
		"You need the basics? Wiki exists. YouTube is drowning in tutorials. Go check those out."
		""
		"Also, a ton of items and machines in Create have a Ponder option. Just hold W while hovering over an item to watch a little blueprint show you exactly how it works. Super handy. Use it."
	]
	quest.157C24B27617DFF7.quest_desc: ["Seriously? You actually did it? You managed to catch every single fish in this frozen wasteland, proving that not even a global ice age can stop you from being the ultimate master of the rod! You’ve survived the minigames, the broken lines, and the freezing water, so wear this achievement with pride—you’re officially the king of the ice holes!"]
	quest.158FB0CCCBB8E433.quest_desc: [
		"A common magic material used in many recipes. Can be found sparsely in vanilla structures, but much more commonly in magic structures or from killing magic mobs."
		""
		"Early spell books are pretty basic, so hunt for mid-game upgrades to get more slots, and grab the Wandering Magician armor if you're tired of running out of mana!"
	]
	quest.15DD42664DDD09DB.quest_desc: ["Can be found below y = -38, unexposed to air. Requires a netherite pickaxe to harvest."]
	quest.161EDD68FF1A7F1B.quest_subtitle: "Runs on lava"
	quest.1630CFBFB562C43B.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.1630CFBFB562C43B.quest_subtitle: "Use liquid fuel to generate power"
	quest.16B0C1F7B951C19D.quest_desc: ["Now we have our &ePackager&r we can now have &ePackages&r! \\n\\nThere is 4 varients but that doesn't change anything with them besides apperance. It is entirely random which one you get. \\n\\n&ePackages&r are &eItems&r and when Placed on the Ground will become Entities. You can Right Click them after they were Placed to Pick them up, or Break them to get the &eItems&r out. You can also move them like any other Entity! \\n\\n&ePackages&r can also be used to interact with other &6Machines&r. Like being placed on &8Chain Conveyors&f or &eBelts&r!"]
	quest.16B0C1F7B951C19D.title: "&eCardboard Packages"
	quest.171255E855338EC7.quest_desc: [
		"Rotational Power is your bread and butter for running Create machines. Drills, mixers, presses—all that good stuff runs on spinny power."
		""
		"But here's the thing. You can also convert that Rotational Power into regular old energy using an Alternator. Hook it up to a shaft, feed it some RPMs, and suddenly you're powering electric machines too."
		""
		"So yeah, windmills, water wheels, steam engines—they're not just for Create anymore. One setup, two uses. Pretty neat, right?"
	]
	quest.171255E855338EC7.title: "Cogwheel!"
	quest.1712C3B3CF158843.quest_desc: ["To make the &ePrecision Mechanism&r we'll need 3 &6Deployers&r, 3 &eDepots&f/&eBelts&r, 1 &eGold Plate&r, 5 Cogs, 5 Large Cogwheels, and 5 &7Iron Nuggets&r, as well as luck! \\n\\nTake your &eGold Plate&r (which can be made from Pressing a Gold Ingot) and place it beneath each of the Deployers in order. \\n\\nThe first will need a Cog, the second will need a Large Cog, and the third will need an Iron Nugget. \\n\\nThen, once it has been processed through all 3 of them, repeat it! And do it 5 times in a row. \\n\\nAt the end, there is only an 80% chance it will actually make it. The other 20% will see all your work going POOF!"]
	quest.1712C3B3CF158843.title: "&ePrecision Mechanism"
	quest.175509632CBF8631.quest_desc: ["Improves yield on all pulverisation recipes."]
	quest.175509632CBF8631.quest_subtitle: "A better pulverizer"
	quest.17EAAC737E5B4FFE.quest_desc: ["Increases the size of your 'fishing bar', making catching fish easier!"]
	quest.1831B35A3239B583.quest_subtitle: "Doing multiple recipes at once"
	quest.18914FDF9CF9EEA8.quest_desc: ["&aClockwork Bearings&r will move based on the Time of Day when given &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThe Block in front of the &aClockwork Bearing&r will automatically &aGlue&r to it, but other Blocks can be &aGlued&r to that Block to join it! \\n\\nIf you want more Hands to your &aClock&r, add more Blocks in front of the first Block, but make sure these aren't &aGlued&r together. \\n\\nYou can change which Hands are which by Holding on the &aBearing&r to change whether the first Hand (closest Block) is the Hour or Minute Hand. "]
	quest.18914FDF9CF9EEA8.title: "&aClockwork Bearing"
	quest.194B832845BB6066.quest_desc: [
		"Need to cook fast? The Skillet is a beast. It processes food 80% faster than a regular campfire (only 6 seconds per item!). But it’s not just a pan—it’s a lifestyle."
		""
		"How to use it:"
		""
		"On the Stove: Place it down (Sneak + Right-click) on a heat source. It can cook a whole stack of items and will pop them off to the side when done. Use a hopper or basket to catch them!"
		""
		"On the Go: Hold it in your hand near any fire, and you can cook items held in your off-hand. You can even cook while you are on fire (though we don't recommend it)."
		""
		"As a Weapon: It hits like an Iron Axe but with double the knockback. BONK!"
		""
		"Pro Tip: You can enchant it like a sword! Fire Aspect actually makes it cook even faster."
	]
	quest.196F31710C031978.quest_desc: ["Runs on lava"]
	quest.19FC97EADC8F20DD.quest_desc: ["Place your backpack on the Shelf to display it and save space."]
	quest.1B182A30604655E2.quest_desc: ["&cBlaze Burners&r are pretty easy to Craft, you'll just need some &7Iron Plates&r with a singular Block of &4Netherrack&r. \\n\\nThen you'll need to use a &oMysterious Conversion&r to make it less Empty! That is just Right Clicking a &cBlaze&r with your &cEmpty Blaze Burner&r. \\n\\nWhen we place him though, he seems a little small and... lukewarm... \\n\\nWe'll need to feed him! No, not Steak, &cBlazes&r don't like Steaks. He'll need either Furnace Fuels like Wood or Coal, or his favorite: the &cBlaze Cakes&r! \\n\\nThe Furnace Fuel will get them only a bit Heated, but the &cBlaze Cakes&r will make them &bSuper-Heated&r! Yes, &bSuper-Heated&r is hotter than &6Orange&r Hot. \\n\\nSome Recipes and &6Machines&r will need to be Heated, like &6Automated Brewing&r, &6Mixing&r, and the Steam Boiler will! "]
	quest.1B182A30604655E2.title: "&cBlaze Burner"
	quest.1B2BD489D5173B40.quest_subtitle: "Loads of ways to get this"
	quest.1B5A12FD501C6E66.quest_desc: [
		"You actually did it."
		""
		"You’ve spent countless hours trekking through the frozen wastes, diving into the deepest caves, and fighting every Mimic in your path. You’ve collected every single artifact in existence."
		"In a world where these relics are nearly impossible to find, you defied the odds. But now that you have them all... Why? Was it for the power? The prestige? Or are you just that obsessed with completing your collection?"
		""
		"Whatever the reason, you are now the most well-equipped survivor this eternal winter has ever seen. Enjoy your rewards, you madman."
	]
	quest.1B6526907DD9B21A.quest_desc: ["Runs on Diesel"]
	quest.1BA11428DF7541AD.quest_desc: ["Because the &eSequenced Gearshift&r uses much fancier &eItems&r it is clearly a much fancier &6Machine&r! \\n\\nJudging by how confusing its GUI is, I'd say so... Hopefully I can help make it less confusing! No promises though. \\n\\nLike the normal &dGearshift&r it will need a &4Redstone Signal&r to do whatever is designed. We'll need to configure its GUI to make a \"script\". \\n\\nFirst, is the Instructions, these are the actual tasks it will preform. Here it can turn its &8Shaft&r, effect a Pulley, wait, or just stop. It will need to stop at the end, it is inevitable. \\n\\nNext, is the Angle. The Angle that either the &8Shaft&r or Pulley will turn. From 360 to 1 degree! \\n\\nLast is the Speed and Direction. It changes how quickly the Shaft or Pulley move and either &e&oClockwise&r or &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r."]
	quest.1BA11428DF7541AD.title: "&eSequenced Gearshift"
	quest.1C2309DB4B890E71.quest_desc: ["&bSpouts&r are used with systems to fill &eItems&r with &bFluid&r. \\n\\nFirst, you'll need to fill the &bSpout&r by &bPiping Fluid&r into it! \\n\\nThen, if there is a &bFluid&r Holding &eItem&r: Bucket or Bottle, then it will be filled with the &bFluid&r in the Spout. \\n\\nIt will automatically fill it, it doesn't need Rotational Power it uses Gravity!"]
	quest.1C2309DB4B890E71.title: "&bSpout"
	quest.1C71A99AA50DC379.quest_desc: ["Runs on... yeah, you know. Not gonna spell it out for you"]
	quest.1C99A17373D24810.quest_desc: [
		"You need a bed. Period."
		""
		"[ \"Did you skip the \", { \"text\": \"Sleep Tight\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1CECA5AA5359EE59\" } }, \" quest? Go back and read it. No, seriously. Read it.\" ]"
		""
		"If you don't understand how sleeping works in this pack, you will die. Maybe not tonight. Maybe not tomorrow. But soon."
		""
		"Your bed is your only respawn point. If you don't have a Home Bed established, you will respawn somewhere you really don't want to be. Probably very, very far from your stuff."
		""
		"Sleep too often? Nightmares. Ten minutes of insomnia. Half the night wasted. Sleep near darkness? Something will wake you up. Personally."
		""
		"Craft a bed. Use it wisely. Or don't. The choice is yours. The consequences are also yours."
	]
	quest.1C99A17373D24810.title: "Bed!"
	quest.1CECA5AA5359EE59.quest_desc: [
		"Sleeping in this frozen world is not a simple escape. It is a calculated risk."
		""
		"Your bed is no longer a safe haven. Sleep too often and Nightmares will rip you from your slumber after only half the night, leaving you with a brutal 10 minute insomnia cooldown. The more consecutive nights you sleep, the higher the chance. After three nights in a row, the real terror begins."
		""
		"Bedbugs lurk in the shadows, waiting to infest your bed and render it useless. Dreamer Essence will not save you from them here."
		""
		"Your only solace is commitment. Sleep in the same bed six times to establish it as your Home Bed. Only then will you receive the Invigorated buff upon waking, increasing XP gained from ores and mobs. But be warned: this is your only respawn point now. If you die far away, you will return to this exact bed. No exceptions."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Hammocks allow you to rest during the day without setting your spawn, but they offer no benefits and still trigger the same cooldowns. Night Bags are a late-game tool for desperate camping, but they too set no spawn and grant no buffs."
		""
		"Hunger is drained based on time slept and difficulty. Healing and effect clearing on wake up are disabled. You wake up exactly as battered as you were when you closed your eyes."
		""
		"Sleep Encounters can still happen if you dare rest near darkness. Mobs will find you."
		""
		"This is not comfort. This is survival."
	]
	quest.1CECA5AA5359EE59.quest_subtitle: "you can get out of bed with shift"
	quest.1CECA5AA5359EE59.title: "Sleep Tight"
	quest.1D472C10B9D15671.quest_desc: ["Here are some bosses and enemies you can defeat. Or if you want, there are more of them... but I don't know, discover the rest yourself as they got lost somewhere."]
	quest.1D6CA4631DAFE469.title: "Skins"
	quest.1D9A00C81C2A97F0.quest_subtitle: "Underwhelming"
	quest.1DBF1D4061518B0B.quest_subtitle: "Turning one into more"
	quest.1DBF1D4061518B0B.title: "Refining Ores"
	quest.1DC532C4E724902E.quest_desc: ["Runs on fuel like diesel, gasoline etc."]
	quest.1DCD856D77287F70.quest_desc: [
		"Rover. Your little space car. Drive it around on pretty much any planet you land on."
		""
		"And just like your rocket, you can Upgrade it. Same system, different vehicle."
		""
		"Way better than walking everywhere."
	]
	quest.1E199A8479E3CCC7.quest_desc: ["Just like the pot, you can place your Frying Pan on the Electric Stove. As long as it has power."]
	quest.1E1D0DD85879E40B.quest_desc: [
		"Got your fire ready? Good. Now you need something to actually mix those proteins and veggies in. Enter the Cooking Pot. This isn't just a pot; it’s a workstation and a portable pantry all in one!"
		""
		"How to use it:"
		""
		"Heat it up: Place it over your Stove or Campfire. If you see bubbles and steam, you're cooking!"
		"Mix and Match: Throw up to 6 ingredients inside. If the recipe is right, it’ll start cooking automatically."
		""
		"Serving: Most meals need a container (like a Bowl). Put them in the container slot or just right-click the pot with one to grab your food."
	]
	quest.1E30A1B49ED83418.quest_desc: ["Snowman!!"]
	quest.1E74C5694AD09362.quest_desc: ["do not have a mining speed penalty when underwater."]
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.quest_desc: ["The &6Encased Fan&r is one of the most underrated Machines in &6&lCreate&r. \\n\\nYou can place it down and it'll face you, or Shift Right Click to place it facing away from you. \\n\\nWhen given &dRotational Power&r &e&oClockwise&r, it will blow air away from it. When given &dRotational Power&r &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r it will suck air toward it. \\n\\nThese sucks and blows will also effect &eItems&r and Entities near them, and yes the faster it spins the more it sucks and blows! \\n\\nWe also get extra Recipes we can make by putting a Block in front of the &6Fan&r. This will then effect the &eItems&r being blown on by the &6Fan&r. \\n\\nWe can use &cLava&r to &6Blast&e Items&r like a Furnace. Getting Ingots from Ores, Stone from Cobble, and Nuggets from Tools. \\n\\nIf we put Fire in front of the Fan we can Smoke Items. Like Cooking them! \\n\\nInstead of Lava we can also place Water in front of it. This will wash whatever is in front of it like Concrete Powder into Concrete. \\n\\nAnd last, instead of Fire we can use Soul Fire to haunt Items! This will change Items either into Nether variants or entirely different Items."]
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.quest_subtitle: "This blows!"
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.title: "&6Encased Fan"
	quest.1EAC5B0385876CBB.quest_desc: [
		"Iron bookshelves. They work just like regular ones, but they pack way more enchanting power."
		""
		"What does that mean? You don't need to surround your table with fifteen bookshelves just to hit level 30. A few of these bad boys will do the job. Less clutter, same magic."
		""
		"And yeah, just like everything else in this pack, you can upgrade them further. Diamond, netherite, whatever. I'm not listing them all. You get the idea."
	]
	quest.1F139091C1B4E50B.quest_subtitle: "A normal circuit"
	quest.1F5A8129B3930C3A.quest_desc: ["Your head is very easy to break, especially if you get shot by a projectile. To minimize the effect arrows have on this limb wear a healmet."]
	quest.1F5A8129B3930C3A.title: "Headshots"
	quest.1FFCE66C9AC1BF59.quest_desc: ["chance to not use durability"]
	quest.20540E758A6F689F.quest_desc: [
		"Winter blizzards are dangerous, but explosions are worse. If you want your loot to be 100% safe, you need the Obsidian Chest."
		"It’s as big as a Diamond Chest, but it’s completely blast-resistant. Not even a Creeper or a stray TNT can destroy your hard-earned supplies in this icy wasteland."
	]
	quest.2074E1CB1568E046.quest_desc: ["deal extra damage underwater."]
	quest.207D5CB20C1CFB6D.quest_desc: [
		"While not strictly required, a Butcher's Table makes your life way easier. It’s the perfect spot to place your drained carcasses for the final cut."
		"Choose your style: go for a classic Wooden Table (Oak, Acacia, etc.) or upgrade to a sleek Metal one. It looks cool and keeps your kitchen organized!"
	]
	quest.208DC83C5E3C4C6F.quest_desc: [
		"Some potions are actually gonna save your life in this pack."
		""
		"Get a brewing stand going. Stock up on blaze powder and awkward potions. You'll thank me later when you're not dead."
	]
	quest.222F9B9A8AEC8001.quest_desc: [
		"If you don't have an Atlas yet, or just want a low-tech solution, use chalks."
		""
		"Mark your path, leave a trail, do whatever you need to not get completely lost in some cave or forest."
		""
		"Simple, cheap, and surprisingly useful. Don't underestimate the power of scribbling on walls."
	]
	quest.222F9B9A8AEC8001.title: "Chalks"
	quest.227B3A61BB36F4E3.quest_desc: ["The Hammer allows you to quickly cycle through different styles for some  furniture pieces and decorative objects in this mod."]
	quest.235E1B8799FB1B4F.quest_desc: ["Store the power you generate"]
	quest.24310BEACE75749D.quest_desc: [
		"Addons function as upgrades as well as modules to &5Oritech&r. "
		""
		"Addons are to be added onto plug like looking slots. Number of addon depends on the machine cores being used."
		""
		""
		"{image:atm:textures/questpics/oritech/ori-addon-slot.png width:50 height:100 align:left}"
		""
		"Addons also add additional functionality to the machines. Sometimes, you will need to add particular addons to allow recipes to work"
	]
	quest.24310BEACE75749D.quest_subtitle: "Making it worth"
	quest.24E658BA47367A44.quest_desc: ["&aRope Pulley&r will move any Blocks that are attached to its &aRope&r at the bottom of it. This will also move any Blocks &aGlued&r to that Block! \\n\\nWhen moved &e&oClockwise&r by &dRotational Power&r, it will lower the &aRope&r until it hits another Block, or to where it is set. \\n\\nWhen given &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r &dRotational Power&r it will move the &aRope&r toward the &aPulley&r until it hits the &aPulley&r or it goes where it is set to go. \\n\\nWhy do I keep saying \"set to go\"? Because there is destination settings with Movement Mode! \\n\\nThese will decide where the Blocks end up stopping!"]
	quest.24E658BA47367A44.title: "&aRope Pulley"
	quest.252CB47834520928.quest_desc: ["Unlocks Chapter: How to Escape the Planet"]
	quest.2572AA3E55216FA8.quest_desc: [
		"The base for all other runes to be crafted from. Can be found rarely in some vanilla structures, or more commonly in magic structures. Each school mage drops one for their school on death."
		""
		"Using 8 focuses, you can craft a runestone to a specific school, and use your inscribed runestone to craft gear related to that school."
	]
	quest.2577C6BBC8F9CF14.quest_desc: [
		"After that, you will need an Oxygen Distributor"
		""
		"Place it in a sealed room with nothing over, and then put the oxygen tank in the middle slot !"
		""
		"The Oxygen Distributor need to be powered."
	]
	quest.27C2D57ED0FBBEDD.quest_desc: ["Once crafted, it finds the nearest Catacombs and leads you towards it"]
	quest.27D3BBB84BD5DE3D.quest_desc: [
		"Watch what you drink! If you drink directly from dirty sources or fill your canteen with unpurified water, it might hydrate you slightly, but there is a 75% chance of contracting the Thirst effect. This will cause your thirst bar to deplete much faster than usual."
		""
		"Temperature also affects your hydration:"
		"When your body heat reaches dangerously high levels, your thirst bar will take on a flame-like appearance. This is the Heat Thirst effect—a clear sign that the scorching heat is draining your fluids rapidly."
		""
		"Keep it cool, and keep it clean."
	]
	quest.27E33C24C9297646.quest_desc: [
		"Ice Fern. You can find these scattered across the world. They are a vital ingredient for crafting Cold String and Cold Resistance potions."
		"Good luck finding them under all that snow... or elsewhere."
	]
	quest.28560BF0BDB2A381.quest_desc: [
		"Want to save that precious blood for sausages? Place a Blood Grate directly under your hanging carcass. It’ll catch every drop!"
		""
		"Pro Tip: If you're using other mods, craft Butcher's Papers and right-click the grate to switch which type of blood it collects."
	]
	quest.28DECDA53CC5B21C.quest_desc: ["Can be used to brew potions, craft elixirs, recycle scrolls, and upgrade ink. If a mob or player is placed in it while there is water, blood vials can also be produced. It has 4 input and 4 output slots, and must have water in it to activate. Right click to place a valid item into the input slots, and right click with a glass bottle to extract an output item."]
	quest.290C1416EA2B5DF2.quest_subtitle: "They seem a bit dry"
	quest.29917E6196649F5D.quest_desc: ["Speed is distance over time, AKA how long it takes to get from point A to point B... well... we are working with &dRevolutions&r, it is more how long it takes to get from point A to point A in this big of a Circle. \\n\\nAnyways it is how quick our &6Machines&r move, including &dCogs&r and &8Shafts&r! \\n\\nThis is important because Speed will effect how other &6Machines&r work. Some will need a certain Speed and others will work more efficiently at higher Speeds. \\n\\nWe can place a Speedometer (yes, like in a car) into our Kinetic System to see how fast everything is moving."]
	quest.29917E6196649F5D.title: "Speed"
	quest.2A3AED5EA21A9152.quest_desc: [
		"Cold Eye - Found in Igloos"
		""
		"One of the last artifacts left behind by the Iceologers before they all suddenly vanished from the world"
	]
	quest.2A69272FD3C57924.quest_subtitle: "Slightly better"
	quest.2AAC1E2ABC81A15C.quest_desc: [
		"Next important thing: fuel for your rocket. To make that happen, you're gonna need oil. "
		""
		"Oil Finder"
		""
		"Craft yourself an Oil Finder. Right click on any block and it'll tell you straight up if there's oil in that chunk. Simple, reliable, gets the job done."
	]
	quest.2B1DD37A14897C46.quest_desc: [
		"Before we go any further, you're gonna need power. And I mean a lot of it."
		""
		"[ \"Check out the \", { \"text\": \"Energy\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"3EB8A6EAD7509DF6\" } }, \" chapter if you haven't already. Plenty of options in there, from basic to overkill.\" ]"
		""
		"I mean, every machine needs electricity, right? That's just... logic."
		""
		"So go get some juice flowing, then come back."
	]
	quest.2B86A2A970106C8A.quest_desc: [
		"you found platinum. Shiny. Heavy."
		""
		"If you use Oritech: Congratulations. This is actually useful. Feed it to your machines. Progress awaits."
		""
		"If you don't use Oritech: This is completely useless to you. You will never craft anything with it. You know this. You're still going to take it."
		""
		"Either way, it's coming home with you."
	]
	quest.2C026F813EE69BE0.quest_desc: [
		"Heals all Body Limbs"
		""
		"Regenerates 8.0 health over 20.0"
	]
	quest.2C2958E38293717E.quest_desc: ["To start with the new &6&lCreate&r &eItems&r we'll need &eCardboard&r! \\n\\nWhich is made from &6Pressing&r Pulp. \\n\\nPulp is made from &6Mixing&r 4 Saplings and &9Water&f in a &6Mechanical Mixer&r and &8Basin&r. \\n\\nYou can combine &eCardboards&r to make &eBlocks of Cardboard&r which can make the new &eItems&r in &6&lCreate&r... or &eCardboard Armor&r!"]
	quest.2C2958E38293717E.title: "&6&lCreate&r 1.21"
	quest.2C6769367153B4D9.quest_desc: [
		"Need salt for those Skins? Craft a Basin."
		""
		"Fill it with water and let the sun do the work. Over about half a Minecraft day, the water evaporates, leaving Salt behind. Just right-click to grab it or use a hopper."
		"Note: It must be outside in direct sunlight. No sun, no salt!"
	]
	quest.2C8DB4ACEC0A2101.quest_desc: ["Use empty bottle on charged creeper"]
	quest.2CF315F4F3277794.quest_desc: ["When you finally found oil in a chunk, you can craft the pumpjack drill and then you will be able to craft the pumpjack"]
	quest.2D41B04C75FA02BC.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Press&r is very helpful for making even more &6Machines&r! \\n\\nWhen powered with &dRotational Power&r (and a lot of Stress Units) it will send the &6Metal Press&r down to Blocks below it. Like a Hydraulic Press! \\n\\nAny Items below it: either on a &eBelt&r, &eDepot&r, or even just dropped, will be &6Pressed&r. \\n\\nThis is mainly for turning &7Ingots &finto &7Plates&r with no charge. You can also use it to get Paper from Sugarcane and Paths from Dirt! \\n\\nIf you place a &8Basin&r beneath it you can then use the &6Press&r to combine &bLiquids&r, &eItems&r, and Blocks to create new &eItems&r. \\n\\nAnother option with the &8Basin&r below our Press is Compacting Crafting. This is automated Crafting for Recipes that contain only one type of &eItem&r, like 9 &7Iron Ingots&f into an &7Iron Block&r."]
	quest.2D41B04C75FA02BC.title: "&6Mechanical Press"
	quest.2D96965317D3CFEC.quest_desc: ["Yay, complicated subjects! This time it is &5Conductors&r and &5Train Schedules&r. \\n\\nFirst is getting our &5Conductor&r, these are any Lead-able Mobs or &cBlaze Burners&r. If we have a Seat next to the Train Controls we can Lead a Mob into the Seat where it will wait to become a &5Conductor&r. \\n\\n&cBlaze Burners&r work similar, just without the need for a seat, they bring their own. \\n\\nThen, we can hand our Mob or &cBlaze Burner&r, a filled out &5Schedule&r to give them that task plus a &5Conductor's Hat&r. \\n\\n&5Schedules&r are Items that can be \"Coded\" to order our &5Conductors&r to preform certain tasks. The tasks are either: go to &5Station&r, pickup or drop off Packages, change title, or change max speed. \\n\\nOnce we add a task, we can edit its configs to change when it will start the next task! These can be either a certain Time waited, Time of Day, amount of stuff in &5Train&r, or even &4Redstone&r!"]
	quest.2D96965317D3CFEC.title: "&5Conductors"
	quest.2D9FB9F0052C93A8.quest_desc: [
		"So here's the thing. This pack has over 110 enchantments. Maybe more. I'm not counting."
		""
		"The RNG is absolutely wild. You want that one specific enchant? Good luck. You're gonna be rolling the dice for a while."
		""
		"Let's see if you can actually get the enchantments you want. If you can even figure out what they all do first."
	]
	quest.2DC59272632EFE0C.quest_desc: [
		"Hang 'Em High!"
		""
		"Before you can turn that carcass into a steak, you’ve got to drain the blood. Nobody likes a messy kitchen, right?"
		""
		"To get started, you’ll need a Hanging Rope or a Hook. Just hang your prey up and right-click the body with a Cleaver to start the bleeding process."
		"Pro Tip: Be careful with the Rope — it’s cheap, but it can snap under too much weight! If you want a setup that actually lasts, go for the Hook. It’s much more reliable when you're dealing with a heavy haul."
	]
	quest.2DC59272632EFE0C.title: "Rope?"
	quest.2DC9CADD921F762A.quest_desc: [
		"Not a fan of following quest lines? "
		"Prefer to figure things out yourself while shivering in the snow? Respect."
		""
		"If you want the full lowdown on every cut of meat and how to properly use your tools without me holding your hand, take this Butchery Guide. It covers everything from bleeding out the carcass to the final steak."
	]
	quest.2DC9CADD921F762A.title: "Guide!"
	quest.2DE98DEC56787ACA.quest_desc: ["Use liquid fuel to generate power"]
	quest.2FC2A8BEBE142129.quest_desc: [
		"When fed to any tamed mount (Horses, Donkeys, Mules, Llamas etc), Horse Feed will fully heal the mount, and grant them the following positive effects:"
		""
		"Speed II (5:00)"
		"Jump Boost (5:00)"
		"This combination allows your mount to be a lot more agile during travels. Since mounts eat a large volume of feed, the item does not need to be contained in a Bowl, saving some inventory space."
		""
		"Horse Feed cannot be fed to Pigs or Striders, as they are not tamed, or cannot eat hay."
	]
	quest.3029E1E133B91ED8.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Drill&r can be used within a &aContraption&r or without. The without will need &dRotational Power&r but still does the same task. \\n\\nThe &6Mechanical Drill&r will Mine any Block in front of it (that it can). \\n\\nIt will Mine as fast as the &dRotational Power&r will give. And if there is an Inventory connected to the &aContraption&r, the Mined Block will be put into it, instead of on the floor. \\n\\nYes, the &6Drill&r has a limit, it only has Diamond Tier for Mining. So, no Mining &6AllTheModium&r!"]
	quest.3029E1E133B91ED8.title: "&6Mechanical Drill"
	quest.308EC5110C18D379.quest_desc: ["You can make fish fillet with a fish filet knife. The amount of fish fillets you get depends on the type of fish."]
	quest.30AC43222FF9B18A.quest_desc: ["&5Train Signals&r are used with &5Conductors&r who aren't Players. \\n\\nThey place just like &5Train Stations&f and &5Observers&r, but the way they are placed determines the Arrow placement. \\n\\nThe Arrows will restrict where &5Conductors&r can pass their &5Trains&r, if the Arrow is facing the opposite way, the &5Train&r won't pass. \\n\\nYou can add two Signals facing opposite directions to let &5Conductors&r pass wherever you want. \\n\\nWith a bunch of &5Signals&r we can make Stop Lights for &7Track&r intersections. Place the &5Signals&r to where there are Arrows on both sides of the intersection. \\n\\nThis will make it so &5Trains&r will stop if another &5Train&r is in the intersection. That prevents collisions which Derail &5Trains&r. Derailed &5Trains&r will need a Wrench to put them back on &7Track&r!"]
	quest.30AC43222FF9B18A.title: "&5Train Signals"
	quest.310FA9380CB3E0BB.quest_subtitle: "Allows additions of fluids to centrifuge"
	quest.312A2E9692D410F0.quest_desc: ["longer opportunity to reel in a fish."]
	quest.3141217F42936F6B.quest_desc: ["Dropped from the Ender Dragon"]
	quest.31BCF971840D1E95.quest_desc: ["[ \"I added almost every item from this mod to this quest (don't ask why, I don’t even know myself... ), but you'll need the Workbench to craft them and power to run the electric ones—check the \", { \"text\": \"generator\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"11AB59E17E25B7B4\" } }, \" quest to see how!\" ]"]
	quest.32CE287E70120A67.quest_desc: [
		"Wither Eye - Dropped by The Wither"
		""
		"Has witnessed destruction. Maybe it also witnessed your stuff disappear"
	]
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.quest_desc: ["&6Deployer&r is a very fun &6Machine&r for poking! \\n\\nBy poking, I mostly mean &eItem Interactions&r that we can preform. Place an &eItem&r into the &6Deployer Hand&r, and then give it &dRotational Power&r. It will then place the &eItem&r into the Block on a &eDepot&f or &eBelt&r below. \\n\\nThis will mimick many actions that we can do, like adding &6Wax&r to &cCopper&r. \\n\\nYou'll most likely use it for &8Andesite&r/&cCopper&r/&eBrass&r Casings and &4Polished Rose Quartz&r."]
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.quest_subtitle: "Poke"
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.title: "&6Deployer"
	quest.334AB2ED426108C7.quest_subtitle: "Call it what you want, it grinds"
	quest.33AEE346859EF57F.quest_desc: [
		"You did it. The great beast is dead. Its body crumbles into nothing, and the End grows quiet."
		""
		"You stand there, waiting. For the fanfare. For the credits. For something. Anything."
		""
		"Nothing happens."
		""
		"The silence is deafening. The sky does not cheer. The world does not care. You have slain a god, and the universe yawned."
		""
		"This is the truth of this frozen reality: your actions change nothing. You are not the hero of this story. You are just another creature, clawing at the void."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"So now you face a choice."
		""
		"Stay. Live out your days in this cold, unforgiving land. Hunt every boss. Conquer every dungeon. Prove to yourself that you can. Not because it matters, but because you refuse to stop."
		""
		"Or run. Find a way off this dying planet. Escape into the unknown. Leave it all behind."
		""
		"There is no right answer. There is no reward. There is only what you decide."
	]
	quest.33AEE346859EF57F.title: "The Dragon Falls"
	quest.33D74D4180DF3CA1.quest_desc: [
		"When fed to any tamed Wolf (your own, or belonging to another player), Dog Food will fully heal the wolf, and grant them the following positive effects:"
		""
		"Speed (5:00)"
		"Strength (5:00)"
		"Resistance (5:00)"
		"This combination allows wolves to catch up a lot more easily with you or nimble opponents, as well as last longer in battle."
	]
	quest.33D7DF88207BF01C.quest_desc: [
		"Compacting drawers are a special stone-colored drawer that auto-convert compressible items. Instead of manually crafting and uncrafting between gold blocks, ingots, and nuggets, put them in a compacting drawer. The drawer will internally maintain a pool of the material, and let you insert or remove the material in any of the shown forms."
		""
		"The compacting behavior applies to any item with a compressed recipe, including redstone, glowstone, wheat, and many others."
	]
	quest.34D6F4D719D28582.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.352DB193EC8E768F.quest_desc: ["audible alert when a fish is approaching."]
	quest.3579603C2BA9F051.quest_desc: [
		"Torches, Campfires, and Lanterns will burn out! Once you place a light source, it will eventually go dark. You'll need to relight it using something like a Flint and Steel or Fire Starter."
		""
		"Because of this, I highly recommend investing in more permanent lighting solutions as soon as possible."
		""
		"You might stumble upon \"permanent\" torches out in the world that never go out. These cannot be crafted, so consider it a stroke of luck if you find one!"
	]
	quest.3579603C2BA9F051.title: "Torches"
	quest.35A64A1221DDC82C.quest_desc: [
		"Then there’s your thirst. That water bar is constantly dropping, and if you let it hit rock bottom, your vision's gonna go all blurry. If it hits zero? Say hello to a slow, painful death from dehydration."
		""
		"How to stay hydrated:"
		""
		"Keep it simple—boil some water and chug it from bottles or a canteen. If you want to feel like a pro, craft some juices; they’re the best way to keep your levels up and stay in the game."
	]
	quest.35B94DA0EC30B1FF.quest_desc: [
		"After that, you will be able to generate oxygen"
		""
		"In the left tanks, hydrogen is generated"
		""
		"In the right tank, oxygen is generated"
		""
		"To fill up an item with oxygen, you can place it under the oxygen tank. For exemple, you can fill Oxygen Tank or a Space Suit."
	]
	quest.360EC3C23E7424E6.quest_desc: [
		"Due to the Curse of the Sky, almost every enchantment and curse is now encrypted."
		"If you want to reveal them, you must place the item or book in an Anvil along with an Amethyst Shard. Only then can you test your luck."
		""
		"Some enchantments have managed to resist the curse, but most have fallen. With over 100+ enchantments waiting to be discovered, will you be the one to break the code?"
	]
	quest.367D56A1DBBED16D.quest_desc: [
		"Magical Eye - Dropped by Evokers"
		""
		"Without this eye, the Evoker has no power"
	]
	quest.3697AAF8F281B247.quest_desc: ["This one's a doozy! So listen carefully! \\n1st is constructing the actual &bSteam Engine&r. The &bFluid Tanks&r will judge how much &9Water&r can be held within it and decide the Level the &bSteam Engine&r will be at. \\n\\nThen, simply attach the &bSteam Engine&r to the side of the &bFluid Tanks&r and it'll become a &bSteam Boiler&r. After, place a &8Shaft&r on the &bSteam Engine&r to get our Mechanical Arm that will give us &dRotational Power&r from it. \\n\\n2nd is a &cHeat Source&r. We'll need a &cHeat Source&r beneath the &bFluid Tanks&r to heat up the &9Water&r. There's quite a few &cHeat Sources&r: Fire, Campfire, Lava, Magma Blocks but &cBlaze Burners&r are the best! \\n\\nThe better the &cHeat Source&r, the more Stress Units! So feed those &cBlaze Burners&r some &cBlaze Cakes&r and you'll be rocking! \\n\\n3rd is &9Water&r. This is the fuel of our &bSteam Engine&r, there wouldn't be Steam without &9Water&r. \\n\\nHowever you &bPipe&r in &9Water&r is your choice, but for &6&lATM10&r I recommend a Sink and &9&lID&r!"]
	quest.3697AAF8F281B247.title: "&bSteam Engine"
	quest.36ACF04795F841B7.quest_desc: [
		" Witch Eye - Craft it using the witch pupil"
		""
		" This pupil is believed to have seen the ancient brewing recipes that were lost in time."
	]
	quest.36C4D25671AA06E1.quest_desc: [
		"This is a &9BETA&r version, so expect some bugs, crashes, or performance hiccups. If you find any issues, know which mod is killing the FPS, or have ideas for new features—let me know in the comments or on our official Discord (link on the project page)."
		""
		"This update adds 150+ new mods, so performance might not be as smooth as before. I’m doing my best to optimize everything, but there’s only so much I can do without stripping away the \"core\" mods and the unique atmosphere of the pack."
		""
		"I’ve already squashed most of the lag-causing bugs, but I know there are still some sneaky mods tanking the FPS that I haven't caught yet. If you have a hunch which ones they are, hit me up!"
		""
		"Pro Tip: If you're getting low FPS and have 24GB+ of RAM, try running a local server. It should give your performance a solid boost!"
	]
	quest.36C4D25671AA06E1.quest_subtitle: "Modpack Information"
	quest.36C4D25671AA06E1.title: "!!Modpack!!"
	quest.36E14090AAC2F8C4.quest_desc: ["[ { \"text\": \"Enchants and Curses\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"360EC3C23E7424E6\" } } ]"]
	quest.381C65B2365676DC.quest_desc: [
		"Nether Eye - Found in Nether Fortresses"
		""
		"It was lost by a demon in the battle between the Aether and the Nether"
	]
	quest.388243394B7F1EA0.quest_desc: [
		"Wait... ice after obsidian? What kind of quest structure is this? I don't even know anymore :)."
		""
		"Anyway, to actually get into the Nether, you're gonna need a Frost Heart. And to make that? You need ice. A lot of diamonds. And a heart."
		""
		"How do you get ice? That's the fun part. Figure it out. Silk Touch is your best bet, if you can find it. Or maybe there's another way..."
		""
		"Not gonna spoil it, but one of the quests in this pack has a hint. Go dig around."
		""
		"Suffer a little. It builds character."
	]
	quest.38CB5044AB3F859B.quest_desc: [
		"Super Glue is exactly what it sounds like. It sticks blocks together so you can move them around as one big Contraption later."
		""
		"To glue stuff, just Right Click on two different blocks. Everything in between them gets glued together automatically. If you mess up or change your mind, Left Click with the glue to undo it."
		""
		"Couple rules though. Blocks have to actually touch—diagonals don't count. No cheating the system."
		""
		"You can also stick already glued chunks onto other glued chunks. Glue for everyone!"
		""
		"One cool thing: blocks that are just sitting next to glued blocks will usually come along for the ride too. Same goes for stuff attached to the surface, like torches or signs. Whole wall moves, the decor moves with it."
	]
	quest.38CB5044AB3F859B.title: "Super-Glue"
	quest.38F4448F9603FE68.quest_subtitle: "2 more steps to greatness"
	quest.3933C5718A649B8C.quest_desc: ["Full diamond armor actually gives you heat resistance. Pretty solid for Nether trips."]
	quest.39442B229EA9C587.quest_desc: [
		"Food and some ingredients have a quality level (0–3), shown as stars above the item, from bronze to diamond, which affects their effects. Higher quality gives more hunger and saturation, as well as better effects after eating."
		""
		"Quality also carries over to crafting – better ingredients increase the chance of a better result. When cooking, a bonus builds up that later raises the chance of higher food quality."
		""
		"Simply put: use the best ingredients you can, because better quality = better effects."
	]
	quest.39442B229EA9C587.title: "Quality Food"
	quest.39A7619B4C5592BE.quest_desc: ["&bItem Drains&r are what we can use to mass extract &bFluid&r from &eItems&r! \\n\\nIf a Bottle or Bucket is thrown on top of the &bDrain&r: either by Belts, Chutes, or Hands, the &bFluid&r will be emptied into the &bDrain&r. \\n\\nThe now empty &eItem&r will then be pushed off the &bDrain&r in the opposite direction, and the &bFluid&r will be sitting in the &bDrain&r waiting to be &bPiped&r out."]
	quest.39A7619B4C5592BE.title: "&bItem Drain"
	quest.39F75A94D3073649.quest_desc: [
		"The Arcane Anvil is the most powerful crafting station, used to level up your scrolls, upgrade armor and spell books, and imbue weapons with spell."
		""
		"Use Ink to buff your spells, but keep it logical: you can't upgrade everything, and Common Ink definitely won't work on Rare spells!"
	]
	quest.3A416285631E3F7E.quest_desc: ["casts further."]
	quest.3A4C62865C7CC862.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Tanks&r can hold &bFluids&r. Like Chests, but for &9Water&r and such! \\n\\nYou can only Input &bFluids&r with Buckets but with &bPipes&r you can Input and Output &bFluids&r from them. \\n\\nEach &bFluid Tank&r can hold 8 Buckets or 8000mB of &bFluid&r. But that number will rise when we combine them! \\n\\nYes, you heard me right! We can place multiple &bFluid Tanks&r next to each other to connect their Inventories. They will stack when placed on top of each other up to 32, or by 2x2 or 3x3."]
	quest.3A4C62865C7CC862.title: "&bFluid Tanks"
	quest.3AF2BC9A0E298882.quest_desc: ["With our &8Andesite Alloys&r we can now make &8Andesite Casing&r. \\n\\nGet some Wood, Strip it with an Axe, and then Right Click the Stripped Wood with the &8Andesite Alloy&r. \\n\\nThat will give us our &8Andesite Casing&r! \\n\\n&8Andesite Casing&r will be needed for many, many, many &6Machines&r! And looks good for decoration."]
	quest.3AF2BC9A0E298882.title: "&6&lMachines"
	quest.3B2C2EE216958131.quest_desc: [
		"Evil Eye - Buy it from a master cleric"
		""
		" A holy talisman said to protect its owner from bad luck"
	]
	quest.3B3B38B17CF5D81C.quest_desc: ["&ePackage Frogports&r are adorable and helpful &6Machines&r used for mixing &ePackages&f and &8Chain Conveyors&r! \\n\\nFirst, Right Click a part of the &8Chain &fon a &8Chain Conveyor&r with the &eFrogport&r in Hand, this will set it as the &eFrogports&r destination. \\n\\nThen, when placed we can mess with its GUI. Here we can change the name of its Address, determine whether it takes and gives &ePackages&r or just gives &ePackages&r. \\n\\nThey have 18 Slots to Hold &ePackages&r for moving. \\n\\nIf the Address of the &ePackage&r doesn't match the Address you gave the &eFrogport&f, the &eFrogport&r will send the &ePackage&r onto the &8Chain Conveyor&r. \\n\\nIf it matches the Address, the &ePackage&r will be taken into the &eFrogport&r. If there is no matching Address the &ePackage&r will just go in circles! \\n\\n&ePackages&r can also be automatically sent and taken from &eFrogports&r with &eFunnels &fand &eBelts&r."]
	quest.3B3B38B17CF5D81C.title: "&ePackage Frogport"
	quest.3B5D75B876E74C1C.quest_desc: [
		"Dreamer essence prevents nightmares in a 5 blocks radius"
		"Additionally phantoms will be attracted to Dreamer Essence and will try to break the block. This allows clever players to lure them away allowing one to not be bothered by them"
	]
	quest.3B6B838AF89140C6.quest_desc: [
		"Butchering is a messy business. If your Butcher's Table or floor is covered in blood, you’ll need to clean it up. Plus, you need to wet those skins after salting them!"
		""
		"You have two options:"
		""
		"Sponge: The pro choice. Durable and reliable."
		""
		"Rag: The budget version. Easy to craft with some Strings but breaks quickly."
		""
		"Pro Tip: To use them, you first need to make them wet! Just right-click a water source or a cauldron to soak your Sponge or Rag."
	]
	quest.3C16A6743F8D2DDA.quest_desc: [
		"You found the portal. You jumped in. Congratulations. You are now officially in over your head."
		""
		"First surprise: you don't land on the main island. You're somewhere in the outer End. Confused? Good. Wander around. Find a Gateway. That's your ticket to the big fight."
		""
		"This is not a quick boss rush. This is a journey. The End is vast, empty, and deeply uninterested in your survival. Get used to it."
		""
		"Oh, and that Elytra you were dreaming about? Nerfed. No boosting until the Dragon is dead. You can glide. You can look pretty. You cannot escape. Not yet."
		""
		"Take your time. Explore. Gather resources. Prepare."
	]
	quest.3C5BA8461A35C4D5.quest_desc: [
		"Water Wheels are your basic automatic Rotational Power generators. Nice and simple."
		""
		"Just plop one down and let water flow over it in one direction. If water runs over both sides at once, it just sits there confused. The direction the water flows decides which way the wheel spins."
		""
		"The regular Water Wheel is just one block big. Gives you a bit of speed but barely any Stress Units."
		""
		"The Large Water Wheel is a chunky 3x3. Way more Stress Units, but spins slower."
		""
		"Mix and match both sizes and you can balance out your Speed and Stress Units however you need."
	]
	quest.3C5BA8461A35C4D5.title: "Wheel"
	quest.3C892B33758B7BA6.quest_desc: ["&dCogs &fand &dLarge Cogs&r can interact with each other to change Speed and Stress! \\n\\nIf you connect a &dCog&r, diagonally from a &dLarge Cog&r, the &dCog&r will double in Speed! This is because the &dLarge Cog&r has more Teeth than the &dCog&r, it takes longer to take a full &dRotation&r. \\n\\nThis also works in the reverse, if you put a &dLarge Cog&r diagonal to a &dCog&r, the &dLarge Cog&r will spin at half Speed. \\n\\nThese will also change the Stress Units from the &dCogs&r. More Speed, more Stress. Less Speed, less Stress."]
	quest.3C892B33758B7BA6.title: "&dCog&r Teamwork!"
	quest.3C91BEDD04966721.quest_desc: [
		"Guardian Eye - Get it by Killing Elder Guardian"
		""
		"It has seen many warriors drown into the depths of the sea"
	]
	quest.3C99017FD32B6DE2.quest_desc: ["&eBrass Casings&r are made the same way as &8Andesite&r and &cCopper Casings&r. Just apply the &eItem&r to Stripped Wood. \\n\\nBut with &eBrass Casings&r giving us some of the most powerful &6Machines&r, it won't be as easy to get as &8Andesite&r or &cCopper&r. \\n\\nThankfully this is &6&lATM10&r so you can make &eBrass&r in many different ways! \\n\\nBut the &6&lCreate&r way would be to throw a &cCopper Ingot&r and &7Zinc Ingot&r into a &8Basin&r below a &6Mechanical Mixer&r, while the &8Basin&r is heated."]
	quest.3C99017FD32B6DE2.title: "&eBrass Casing"
	quest.3CAE10287A64CB8D.quest_desc: [
		"Speaking of the Nether... When exploring this fiery dimension, having a Nether Chalice with you can be a lifesaver. It allows you to drink directly from lava to stay hydrated."
		""
		"It might sound crazy, but in the heat of the Nether, it's the ultimate survival tool."
	]
	quest.3D2A03EB2B91E9C1.quest_desc: ["These are literally just fancy Hoppers. \\n\\nThey connect two Inventories, bringing &eItems&r from the Top one to the Bottom one. \\n\\n&eChutes&r can connect to each other, even diagonally. \\n\\nYou can also use them with &6Fans&r to shoot &eItems&r up the &eChutes&r!"]
	quest.3D2A03EB2B91E9C1.title: "&eChute"
	quest.3D5457F29E79EC88.quest_desc: ["Provides better protection against the cold than leather."]
	quest.3D5457F29E79EC88.title: "Snow armor"
	quest.3D7B3F3D1A4662A8.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, this thing lets you craft some cool stuff, but let's be real—you're probably making it because you want to get to the End, right?"
		""
		"Yeah, about that. Hate to break it to you. To even open the portal, you need 12 different types of eyes. Twelve. Not one. Not the same one stacked. Different ones."
		""
		"So before you even think about fighting the dragon, you've got some collecting to do. Good luck out there."
	]
	quest.3D8E824BE61E62B9.quest_desc: ["You can upgrade drawer capacity like chests and barrels or use special keys to lock and manage your items. These tools allow you to automate your storage with features like voiding excess resources and more."]
	quest.3DD27DED791C6A0B.quest_desc: ["To process ores using &5Oritech&r, you need to use a &aCentrifuge&r with a &6Fluid Addon&r and a &aPulveriser&r or &6Fragment Forge&r."]
	quest.3DD27DED791C6A0B.quest_subtitle: "Maximum output"
	quest.3DD27DED791C6A0B.title: "Ore Processing"
	quest.3EB34CC8A3B0DB3C.quest_subtitle: "Doesn't work as hamster feed"
	quest.3EB8A6EAD7509DF6.quest_desc: [
		"This world used to be simple. Just your average magical land, nothing too crazy. Then the sky decided it had enough of being a background decoration."
		""
		"The sky is no longer part of this world. It has become its judge."
		""
		"And here's the problem: everything is under its control. Magic? Watched. Steam power from Create? Monitored. Particle energy from Oritech? You guessed it, still under the sky's thumb."
		""
		"The scientists figured it out pretty quick. There's no loophole. No way to break free while staying here. So their last big idea was to just leave. Pack up and shoot for the stars, somewhere beyond the sky's reach entirely."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"They ran out of time."
		""
		"But hey, you're still here. Maybe you'll pull it off."
		""
		"Either way, you're gonna need power. Basic setups, advanced generators, your call. Electric boilers, machines, whatever you end up building—it all needs juice."
		""
		"Pick your path and let's see how far you get."
	]
	quest.3EB8A6EAD7509DF6.quest_subtitle: "Energy – From Steam to Particles"
	quest.3EB8A6EAD7509DF6.title: "Energy!"
	quest.3EC93F92DF61E8F9.quest_desc: [
		"Black Eye - Found in Buried Chests"
		""
		"Pirates say it gave sight to the legendary Black Pearl"
	]
	quest.3F02EF19112D23BE.quest_desc: ["You'll need &6Mechanical Crafters&r to make the &6Crushing Wheels&r, they are too big for a 3x3 Crafting Table. You'll also need a ton of &8Andesite Alloys&r. \\n\\nBTW, you'll need 2 to actually use them. \\nOnce you have 2, place them next to each other. Then, feed them both &dRotational Power&r and a lot of Stress Units. \\n\\nMake sure that the &6Crushing Wheels&r are spinning in opposite directions or else it won't &6Crush&r! The left one must be spinning &e&oClockwise&r, and the right one must spin &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\nOnce they are spinning (fast and in the right directions) you can have &eItems&r Dropped in between them and they will be &6Crushed&r. \\n\\nWhat &eItems&r? &6Crushed&r Ores from Ores, &eItems&r from Stones and Netherrack, Sand and Flint from Gravel, and even Netherwart from Netherwart Blocks!"]
	quest.3F02EF19112D23BE.title: "&6Crushing Wheels"
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.quest_desc: ["&6Mechanical Arms&r must be configured before Placing them, like the &eWeighted Ejector&r. \\n\\nIt has a 4 Block Range and can pick up from &eBelts &fand &eDepots&r. It can also deposit into &eBelts&f, &eDepots&f, and &eFunnels&r. \\nWhile Holding the &6Mechanical Arm&r, Right Click Blocks to set as Input, then Click again to change it to Output. You can Left Click to deselect the Blocks. You can select as many are in range! \\n\\nOnce it has &dRotational Power&r, an &eItem&r in any Input Block, and space in any Output Block, it will start moving &eItems&r. It will go faster the more Speed is given to it. \\n\\nLike the &eBrass Tunnel&r, the &6Mechanical Arm&r has Distribution Modes. Thankfully a lot less! Round Robin: will go in order for Inputs and Outputs. Forced Round Robin: will wait until every Output has space or every Input has &eItems&r available. Prefer First Target: will go for the closest Block to it."]
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.quest_subtitle: "Why do it yourself when Robot can do it better?"
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.title: "&6Mechanical Arm"
	quest.3F663416E824720C.quest_desc: ["&cCopper Casings&r will be needed for most Machines involved in &bFluid Logistics&r. \\n\\nYou wanna place &9Water&r? You'll need &cCopper Casings&r. You wanna pick up &9Water&r? You'll need &cCopper Casings&r. \\n\\nThey are made just like &8Andesite Casings&r, apply a &cCopper Ingot&r to a Stripped Log."]
	quest.3F663416E824720C.title: "&cCopper Casings"
	quest.3FBCBBEBB78B83FC.quest_desc: ["Finally make a &5Train&r! \\n\\nWe should have our &5Boogeys&r from the &5Train Station&r Quest, no the design of &5Boogey&r doesn't matter. \\n\\nThen, we can place Blocks onto the &5Boogey&r with &aSuper-Glue&r. It doesn't matter what Blocks, pretty much any Block that can be moved can be &aGlued&r! \\n\\nThis is when you try and make it look pretty! Check out Artwork-Builds Showoff in Discord to see a few of them. \\n\\nThe most important Block for our &5Train&r is the &5Train Controls&r. You'll need one in order to actually move the &5Train&r. \\n\\nYou can also add a &5Seat&r for &5Conductors&r (more on that later) or even yourself! \\n\\nOnce it is all ready, just hit \"Assemble Train\" and either your &5Train&r will be made, or it will tell you what you did wrong!"]
	quest.3FBCBBEBB78B83FC.title: "Constructing &5Trains"
	quest.3FD9260DC531CB3D.title: "Random Potion"
	quest.4070BA7A98F2608D.quest_desc: ["chance to catch two things. (10%)"]
	quest.411FD8AA17396F53.quest_desc: [
		"Cutting Board: Essential for slicing food into portions and combining multiple ingredients into one."
		""
		"When preparing meals on the Cutting Board, remember to stack your ingredients from bottom to top: start with your container (like a bowl), then add the main ingredients like wheat etc."
	]
	quest.418E0A23EC74F320.quest_desc: ["An important machine for your future endeavours."]
	quest.418E0A23EC74F320.quest_subtitle: "You spin my head right round..."
	quest.4194397DFD0199C2.quest_desc: ["&6Mechanical Crafters&r can be used for &6Auto-Crafting&r and Recipes that are bigger than 3x3 Crafting Grid like the &6Crushing Wheel&r. \\n\\nPlace the &6Mechanical Crafters&r in the order that is needed, then you'll need to set which direction the &eItems&r in the recipe go. \\n\\nThe direction is known by the arrows on the edge of the &6Crafters&r. These can be changed by Right Clicking them with a &6Wrench&r! \\n\\nThen, just place &eItems&r into the &6Mechanical Crafters&r either with your Hands or automated with &eFunnels&r. \\n\\nAfter that, you can supply &dRotational Power&r to any of the &6Mechanical Crafters&r (they share &dCogs&r) to start up the Recipes. \\n\\nIf it isn't working, check to make sure every &eItem&r is in, every arrow is facing the right way, and it has enough &dRotational Power&r."]
	quest.4194397DFD0199C2.title: "&6Mechanical Crafter"
	quest.41E0A89BB70A10E4.quest_desc: [
		"Don't feel like slicing and dicing? Just use the Spit Roaster."
		""
		"Once the blood is drained, slap the whole carcass onto the spit over a lit campfire. It’s the easiest way to cook a massive amount of food at once without extra prep."
	]
	quest.41FB827C452F59C8.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, I see you're rushing cobblestone already. Classic move."
		""
		"You need it. Stone tools, a furnace—basic survival stuff. If you can't find coal anywhere nearby, just throw some logs in the furnace and make charcoal. Works the same."
		""
		"The furnace also gives off a little heat while it's running. Nothing crazy like a campfire, but it's something."
		""
		"Oh, and if you didn't read the other quests—everything smelts twice as slow in furnace. Painful, I know. You'll want to upgrade to something better eventually."
	]
	quest.4285510271B5223D.quest_desc: ["The &dGearbox&r is helpful for sending &dRotational Power&r in a whole bunch of different directions! \\n\\nThe normal &dGearbox&r will have 4 internal &8Shafts&r, on each of the Cardinal Directions: North, East, South, and West. \\n\\nThe other &8Shafts&r will match the Speed and Stress Units but they will also spin in different directions from the original &8Shaft&r."]
	quest.4285510271B5223D.title: "&dGearbox"
	quest.42DB3BA6D585453C.quest_desc: [
		"But hold up. Before you can even use campfire, you need something to light it with. Can't just stare at it and hope, you know?"
		""
		"You got two options. Flint and Steel is the classic move, but that requires iron and you probably don't have that yet. The cheaper option is a Fire Starter. Way easier to craft, but you'll need some string."
	]
	quest.42DB3BA6D585453C.title: "Light it"
	quest.42F2E7430EE67F9F.quest_desc: [
		"Don't want to empty your chest just to make it bigger? Use an Upgrade Item!"
		"In this frozen wasteland, time is precious. Craft an upgrade and Right-Click on an existing chest to instantly expand its slots. It keeps all your items inside safe and sound while making more room for your winter loot."
	]
	quest.42F5F4F7B307F66A.quest_desc: ["Controller IO blocks act as an extension of a drawer controller, exposing more faces for attaching machines, pipes, or crafting frames. Controllers will bind to an IO when they find them on the network, and all IOs bound to the same controller will share the same inventory and range as that controller. Unlike drawers, IOs cannot be shared, and you should be careful to not put them in range of multiple controllers. Using controller IO is better for performance than using multiple controllers."]
	quest.43064B624A94628B.quest_desc: [
		"Think vanilla mobs are still pushovers? Think again."
		""
		"The monsters in this world have grown smarter. For example, Skeletons will no longer start fighting each other if they accidentally get hit by a stray arrow. Their focus is now entirely on you."
		""
		"As for the other mobs and their new tricks? Well... you’ll have to see for yourself. :)"
		""
		"PS: Even the animals have lost their patience. If you hit them, don't expect them to just run away—they will fight back now."
	]
	quest.43064B624A94628B.title: "Vanilla mobs"
	quest.430F0531123292E6.quest_desc: ["You can craft a Calendar to check the current season... honestly, I’m not sure why you’d bother, but if you really need to see it for yourself, nobody’s stopping you! :)"]
	quest.430F0531123292E6.title: "What is the Season?"
	quest.431626C9E5780322.quest_desc: [
		"Halfway to the century club."
		""
		"Your corpse has been in more places than most tourists. You've personally tested every single way to die in this pack. Quality assurance, they call it. You're doing important work."
		""
		"The bedbugs know you by name. Nightmares have you on speed dial. The cold doesn't even bother introducing itself anymore."
	]
	quest.431626C9E5780322.quest_subtitle: "come back when you die this many times"
	quest.431626C9E5780322.title: "50"
	quest.43625DC301DC6C32.quest_desc: [
		"So, you’ve got the Coal Generator, but how do you actually get the power to where it needs to go? You need a Wrench."
		""
		"This tool is the key to your electrical setup. Use the Wrench to link the generator directly to any block that needs juice. Just point, click, and get the power flowing—no complicated wires needed!"
	]
	quest.438937A39EB0EDA9.quest_desc: ["land hoe'd with this item will always be hydrated."]
	quest.443C7E9F8AA2A83A.quest_desc: [
		"There are 9 schools of magic, and you require a magical focus to craft scrolls or gear pertaining to that school. The schools and their focus are:"
		""
		"Fire - Blaze Rods (Vanilla)"
		"Ice - Frozen Bones (Dropped from Strays)"
		"Lightning - Bottles o’ Lightning - (Use empty bottle on charged creeper)"
		"Holy - Divine Pearls (Crafted from gold and amethyst)"
		"Blood - Blood Vials (Obtained by cooking mobs in a cauldron; put them (or yourself) into a cauldron with a lit campfire beneath them)"
		"Ender - Ender Pearls (Vanilla)"
		"Evocation - Emeralds (Vanilla)"
		"Void - Echo Shards (Vanilla)"
		"Poison - Poisonous Potatoes (Vanilla, with additional recipe)"
	]
	quest.44A448DD37DA0944.quest_desc: [
		"Heals all Body Limbs"
		""
		"Regenerates 5.0 health over 30.0s"
	]
	quest.45581ECB517600C8.quest_desc: ["Fluid tanks work pretty much like power banks, just for liquids instead of energy."]
	quest.46189D4F3B0C0EDB.quest_desc: [
		"Here's how these work. You kill animals, get some animal fat, and craft it with an oil can to fill that bad boy up."
		""
		"Then you use that oil can to fuel your lanterns. Light them up with flint and steel and you've got yourself some proper lighting."
		""
		"A bit more work than torches, but hey, they don't burn out on you. Worth it."
	]
	quest.4694F47980000BE0.quest_desc: ["The base for all other upgrade orbs to be crafted from"]
	quest.46A2DD91AA594A0D.quest_desc: [
		"Look, I'm not gonna sugarcoat it. You're naked, you're vulnerable, and the sky literally wants to kill everything that moves."
		""
		"Start with wood. Punch a tree. You know the drill."
		""
		"Without it, you're not surviving the first night. Or the second. Or any night really."
	]
	quest.46A2DD91AA594A0D.title: "Classic start"
	quest.46D0A19DC3102967.quest_desc: [
		"From now on, you must watch your diet. Food provides various nutrients, so you can't just eat the same thing all the time. Your best bet is to maintain a diverse diet and keep all your levels in check (press N to check your stats)."
		""
		"A well-balanced diet grants you powerful buffs, while overindulging or lacking specific nutrients will result in debuffs. Vegetables are always helpful, and while sugar isn't required, you must make sure your levels don't get too high."
	]
	quest.46D0A19DC3102967.title: "diet?"
	quest.46D3F4AB285A1944.quest_desc: [
		"You want an enchanting setup? Cool. You're gonna need leather for that book."
		""
		"If you're clueless about where to get it, here's your options:"
		""
		"Find it in loot chests. Luck-based, but hey, free is free."
		""
		"[ \"Take the \", { \"text\": \"bloody path\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"67431886C2D8BCE2\" } }, \". Cows, horses, whatever moves. You know what to do.\" ]"
		""
		"Find a whole book in a village or some structure. Skip the crafting entirely."
	]
	quest.46EE72FD95F7BC3B.quest_desc: ["Obtained by cooking mobs in a cauldron; put them (or yourself) into a cauldron with a lit campfire beneath them"]
	quest.472A707806A61028.quest_desc: ["Sama nazwa wskazuje dzialnie tej mikstury :|"]
	quest.474D3FA59B8ED746.quest_desc: [
		"You got wood. Cool. Now you need coal."
		""
		"Why? Two reasons. One: you don't wanna freeze to death like an idiot. Two: you actually want to cook that raw meat before it rots in your pocket."
		""
		"A campfire is your best friend early on. Cheap, simple, keeps you warm and your food edible."
		""
		"Go find some coal. Underground, in cliffs, wherever. Just get it."
	]
	quest.474D3FA59B8ED746.title: "Coal"
	quest.476C7317510198D9.quest_desc: ["Okay this ones fun! You like throwing &eItems&r? Like, I mean to really throw them! \\n\\nThen, the &eWeighted Ejector&r is for you! \\n\\nFirst, you need to Shift Right Click a Block with the &eWeighted Ejector&r to set it as the target. The target has to be in line with where the &eEjector&r is aimed in order to hit it. \\n\\nOnce it has a target and is placed down, it can be fed &dRotational Power&r to charge it! Then, when an &eItem&r is placed on the &eWeighted Ejector&r, it will throw it! \\nYou can hold on some of the Sides to change the Stack Size needed to throw &eItems&r."]
	quest.476C7317510198D9.title: "&eWeighted Ejector"
	quest.47897D827C50629D.quest_desc: ["&aPiston Extension Poles&r are how we can make and expand &aMechanical Pistons&r. \\n\\nNot normal Pistons, sorry!"]
	quest.47897D827C50629D.quest_subtitle: "Why only move so far?"
	quest.47897D827C50629D.title: "&aPiston Extension"
	quest.4789AFE995425C5F.quest_desc: ["Did you know? You can also place your Cooking Pot on top of the Electric Stove. Once it’s powered up, it works just like a regular stove. High-tech cooking at its finest!"]
	quest.4789AFE995425C5F.title: "Stove"
	quest.47A6769B6BF1A46D.quest_desc: ["&eFunnels&r are like if a Hopper and Dispenser had a baby. \\n\\nWhen placed onto a Block with an Inventory, like Chests, it will automatically take &eItems&r out 1 at a time. \\nIf you Shift Right Click it will automatically take &eItems&r into the Inventory. \\n\\nBoth can be turned off with a &4Redstone Signal&r!"]
	quest.47A6769B6BF1A46D.title: "&eAndesite Funnel"
	quest.481311E0030FA4D3.quest_desc: [
		"How to make your base survivable so you don’t freeze to death (or fry)?"
		""
		"If your base is located in a biome with a harsh temperature, you can craft the Ice Box to cool it down or the Boiler to heat it up. These use fuel—snowballs and coal, respectively—and can be toggled on and off with a redstone signal."
		""
		"Pro tip: Use a lever to save fuel when the temperature is just right!"
	]
	quest.483892F0A0F75B97.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Pipes&r are what we'll use to actually move &bFluids&r automatically from one Inventory to another! \\n\\nYou can place them down and they will automatically connect to Inventories and other &bPipes&r. \\n\\nWith a Wrench you can add Windows to a &bPipe&r. These won't connect to parallel &bPipes&r without Windows. \\n\\nThe &bPipes&r themselves won't move &bFluids&r though, we'll need a &bMechanical Pump&r for that! \\n\\nWhen we do get &bPipes&r to start flowing though, we can use them to take &bFluids&r out from a Source Block or the opposite with placing down Source Blocks. \\n\\nThe &bPipe&r will need to have an Open End to do so though, so there can't be Blocks in the way."]
	quest.483892F0A0F75B97.title: "&bFluid Pipe"
	quest.484CAB4E04E8ED49.quest_desc: [
		"Finally. With this stuff, you can make eternal torches. No more replacing burnt out sticks every five minutes."
		""
		"Want permanent campfires? Go for it. Other eternal light sources? Yeah, you got options now."
		""
		"Glowstone opens up way better lighting. Invest in it and stop living in the dark ages."
	]
	quest.48BE7DAC5082044D.quest_desc: ["Stress, like &dRotational Power&r, is important and confusing. \\n\\nStress Units (Su) are power loads for our &6Machines&r. Some &6Machines&r will have a minimum Stress, that means you'll need that much Stress in your System to work the &6Machine&r. \\n\\n&6Deployers&f, &6Mechanical Saws&f, and &6Encased Fans&r are examples of those! \\n\\nSome &6Machines&r also have a maximum Stress Units. That means if it goes over the amount, it will most likely stop working. Or blow up, either or! \\n\\nStress Units are developed from &dCogs&r and from our &6Machines&r that make &dRotational Power&r. &9Water Wheels&r give little Stress while &dSteam Engines&r can give a ton!"]
	quest.48BE7DAC5082044D.title: "Stress"
	quest.48FC18DDF7D5728E.quest_desc: ["From now on, smelting items takes twice as long as usual. Every item now burns for 2x longer, making a better furnace a massive upgrade for your base."]
	quest.495B0CC178B4CFA9.quest_desc: ["The &eBrass Funnel&r is placed and used similar to the &eAndesite Tunnel&r. \\n\\nBut each side comes with new configs! \\n\\nThe Input Side will now come with a Filter option. Just place the &eItem&r in, and it will only take in that &eItem&r. \\n\\nThe Output Side will now come with a limit. You can Scroll to set a number from 1 to 64. You can also choose whether it will Output exactly that amount, or up to that amount. \\n\\nIf it is exactly that amout, it will wait until that amount is within the Inventory to Output it. If it is up to, it will keep Outputting &eItems&r until that number is reached."]
	quest.495B0CC178B4CFA9.title: "&eBrass Funnel"
	quest.497AF307A62E2183.quest_desc: ["The Crystal Chest lets you see exactly what's inside without even opening it. It has the same huge capacity as a Diamond Chest, but it’s completely transparent. Perfect for finding your  medicine quickly!"]
	quest.49D03933633D6A45.quest_subtitle: "It's AI"
	quest.4A093196EAAB88D1.title: "Meat"
	quest.4A209DFCDD17143A.quest_desc: ["Dropped from Strays"]
	quest.4AEFB2B0EC8A02D0.quest_desc: [
		"I'm curious... do you have life insurance?"
		""
		"No? Interesting. Well, here's something. Maybe it'll save you. Maybe it'll make things worse. Maybe it's just a carrot."
		""
		"You clicked. You get what you get. The cold doesn't offer refunds."
	]
	quest.4AEFB2B0EC8A02D0.title: "Random Main"
	quest.4B874A8F00A97E5E.quest_desc: [
		"Shiel Hearts:"
		""
		"Consuming Golden Apples will give you a shield heart."
	]
	quest.4C0E93C937A2E130.quest_desc: ["Increased luck."]
	quest.4C36A78AC7A841A0.quest_desc: [
		"Lost Eye - Found in Mineshafts"
		""
		"It is told that it was forged by the first blacksmiths of time"
	]
	quest.4CBFD7CD025FAB52.quest_desc: ["You actually went through all those items? Absolute legend! Your base is officially the flex of the century – now go show off that designer palace!"]
	quest.4CFA7EE8174E3FD8.quest_subtitle: "Increase energy input rate"
	quest.4D198685B9D759C5.quest_desc: [
		"Corrupted Eye - Found in Pillager Outposts"
		""
		"The eye of a greedy king faded in solitude. Legend says it will bring infinite fortune to its owner"
	]
	quest.4D873B80E889A2A1.quest_desc: [
		"You killed the Wither? On this modpack?"
		""
		"Congrats? I guess?"
		""
		"Honestly, I'm a little impressed. And a little concerned about your mental state. But hey, you got the nether star. Now go craft something ridiculous with it."
	]
	quest.4D8D684669E89D5F.quest_desc: [
		"Considering how freezing cold the End is, and the general difficulty of this pack... yeah, you're probably gonna need this set."
		""
		"Full netherite armor is basically mandatory unless you find some other way to not die out there. Your game, your funeral."
		""
		"Good luck with the ancient debris grind."
	]
	quest.4EAD06B0B3AD7D6E.quest_subtitle: "Fragment raw ores"
	quest.4EAD06B0B3AD7D6E.title: "Clumps"
	quest.4EB89C21DB90D36D.title: "Heads"
	quest.4ED29ACF4A699E1B.quest_subtitle: "Its betterer"
	quest.4F89C04CEBF812F9.quest_subtitle: "Smelt gems into ingots"
	quest.4F89C04CEBF812F9.title: "Ingots"
	quest.4FB61947563CDC57.title: "Knives"
	quest.5007019D9219BE9A.quest_desc: [
		"Iron furnace. Smelts stuff a bit faster than the stone one. Nothing revolutionary, but hey, every second counts."
		""
		"And just like chests, you can upgrade these furnaces later. Better materials, better speed, more slots. Same idea."
		""
		"[ \"I'm not gonna dump every furnace variant on you here. Check the \", { \"text\": \"Storage\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"5568B9ECFF432568\" } }, \" chapter if you want the full rundown. You'll get it.\" ]"
	]
	quest.50232C30F3E68428.quest_desc: [
		"The Nether reaches temperatures much higher than 35.0°C, meaning that you will constantly receive damage by Heat Stroke if you come here unprepared."
		""
		"The End drops the temperature below 0°C, meaning that you will constantly receive damage by hypothermia if you come here unprepared."
	]
	quest.50938AE80704E3D9.quest_desc: ["I heard that Golems have learned how to fight players because of this winter... but is it the truth or just a rumor? Why don't you go check? (ps. you don't have to, and I highly recommend you don't)."]
	quest.50938AE80704E3D9.title: "Iron Golem?"
	quest.50AA119BFD1A39D6.quest_desc: [
		"Don't want to empty your chest just to make it bigger? Use an Upgrade Item!"
		"In this frozen wasteland, time is precious. Craft an upgrade and Right-Click on an existing chest to instantly expand its slots. It keeps all your items inside safe and sound while making more room for your winter loot."
	]
	quest.50DBB87E53017E60.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Valves&r can be used to stop &bPipes&r from moving &bFluid&r. \\n\\nGive them a Rotation, most likely from a &cValve Handle&r, to stop moving &bFluids&r. \\n\\nJust Rotate it again to get the &bFluids&r back!"]
	quest.50DBB87E53017E60.title: "&bFluid Valve"
	quest.51106230B12884CB.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.5134C81D96C55375.quest_desc: ["&5Train Observers&r work like a fancy Detection Rail. \\n\\nWhen a &5Train&r rolls over it the &7Track&r it is set to (which is chosen like the &5Train Station&r) it will give a &4Redstone Signal&r. \\n\\nYou can also place Filters into the &5Observer&r to only get &4Redstone Signals&r when the &5Train&r has that &eItem &for &bFluid&r within."]
	quest.5134C81D96C55375.title: "&5Train Observer"
	quest.5189D72ED3808DC6.quest_desc: [
		"&aShift right-click&r your target designator on the amethyst cluster and then &ashift right-click&r the laser to set the target."
		""
		"These little crystals do more than just look good. They can store energy and used to make more complex machinery."
	]
	quest.5189D72ED3808DC6.quest_subtitle: "Charge amethyst with the laser"
	quest.51EA6B1452883AB2.quest_desc: ["Linear Chasis work like Puddy in real life, only connecting to each other. \\n\\nLinear Chasis, which are facing the same way, will automatically connect as if they were Glued. Other Linear Chasis or ones facing different ways, will not stick together. \\n\\nYou can then use Glue on the Top and Bottom of the Linear Chasis to connect a line of Blocks from it. So all Blocks on top of those will be Glued to the Linear Chasis. Very helpful for saving Glue! \\n\\nWith the Wrench you can set how many Blocks get Glued on the Top or Bottom of the Linear Chasis."]
	quest.51EA6B1452883AB2.title: "&aLinear Chasis"
	quest.520439D1380CC9B7.quest_desc: ["You have two choices for item transport in this eternal winter. Oritech pipes are more efficient and cause less lag in big machines but they require Nickel to craft. Classic pipes are cheaper and show items moving inside but they can lower your FPS and require two types of pipes to work properly  which are Extract and Basic and redstone power. Choose the system that fits your base best."]
	quest.526EBF6588517496.quest_desc: [
		"Got your space suit? Cool. Now make it actually good."
		""
		"The Upgrade Station is where you slap modules onto your space suit and get more abilities."
	]
	quest.52E7D7B706BB0939.quest_desc: [
		"Emeralds. Fancy green rocks. How do you get them?"
		""
		"You got options. Mine them up from deep underground. Find them in chests while exploring. Or trade with villagers."
		""
		"Wait, villagers? Yeah... good luck with that one. It's gonna be rough, but there's a chance."
		""
		"Just don't expect them to hand it over easily. The sky isn't exactly kind to them these days."
	]
	quest.52EED3089D8D8A61.quest_desc: ["casts shorter."]
	quest.531821D544F16FD3.quest_desc: [
		"This little gadget is actually pretty sick. It tells you everything you need to know."
		""
		"Block info? Got it. Items from mods? Covered. Planets? Yep. Mobs? Sure thing."
		""
		"It also tracks how many kilometers you've flown, how many rocket launches you've done, and even how many bosses you've taken down."
	]
	quest.53640172EF904B7D.quest_desc: ["The world is packed with magical loot, so raid structures for scrolls, but make sure you have a spell book first so you can slam them into the Inscription Table and start casting!"]
	quest.53880926982968FD.quest_subtitle: "Say my name"
	quest.53B601A87E8F087F.quest_desc: [
		"To place your rocket, you need 9 Rocket Launch Pad and create this structure."
		""
		"Then, you just need to right click on the launch pads with your Rocket"
	]
	quest.53D5A6F210DF199C.quest_subtitle: "Smoothly transfer 10k rf/t"
	quest.53D5A6F210DF199C.title: "Transfering Energy"
	quest.54A88CA329F0B86F.quest_desc: [
		"1 Body Limb"
		""
		"Regenerates 2.0 Health over 30.0s"
	]
	quest.54E7A9FF9766A3A1.quest_desc: ["The Crystal Chest lets you see exactly what's inside without even opening it. It has the same huge capacity as a Diamond Chest, but it’s completely transparent. Perfect for finding your  medicine quickly!"]
	quest.54EC1C7FC1DA9107.quest_desc: ["&dAdjustable Chain Drives&r work like &dEncased Chain Drives&r, just with more configs. \\n\\nIf we send a &4Redstone Signal&r to the &dAdjustable Chain Drive&r that the original &8Shaft&r is connected to, the other &dChain Drive &8Shafts&r will double in Speed! \\n\\nIf we send one to a different &dChain Drive&r though, the Speed of that &dChain Drive&r will be cut in half!"]
	quest.54EC1C7FC1DA9107.title: "&dAdjustable Chain Drive"
	quest.5568B9ECFF432568.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the Storage chapter! In this eternal winter, keeping your resources organized is the key to survival."
		""
		"In this section, you will learn everything about storing your items, from basic wooden crates to reinforced metal chests. Follow these quests to expand your inventory space and keep your loot safe from the frost."
		""
		"Iron Chests mod has chests for the various metals in vanilla minecraft with varying sizes!"
	]
	quest.5568B9ECFF432568.title: "Chest"
	quest.559A233829B33771.quest_desc: [
		"Wait, they added this in a newer version? Not the one this pack is on... but somehow it's here anyway. Mods are magic, I guess."
		""
		"You can have a friend. A floating, smiling, rideable friend. It's also another way to get around—up to four people can pile on this thing and fly . Great for building high up too since it just stays put when you stand on it."
		""
		"Yeah, it takes some time to rehydrate and grow, but worth it"
	]
	quest.55DCCC4035B8BB2A.quest_subtitle: "Mix netherite and platinum"
	quest.56A7EF9623EEC16B.quest_desc: [
		"Thermal Coats grant Thermal Resistance that will grant you resistance towards Cold and Heat at the same time, these coats are more expensive than the rest."
		""
		"Common Thermal Coat:"
		""
		"Increase the Thermal Resistance by 2.0"
		""
		"Rare Thermal Coat:"
		""
		"Increase the Thermal Resistance by 3.0"
		""
		"Epic Thermal Coat:"
		""
		"Increase the Thermal Resistance by 4.0"
	]
	quest.574ABC9304F86346.quest_desc: [" Can be found in Ancient Cities"]
	quest.574D0F1026B1F96A.title: "Random Enchanted Book"
	quest.57A18F2E51952EB8.quest_desc: ["&5Postboxes&r will use Addresses and &5Trains&r to deliver &ePackages&r! \\n\\nFirst, &ePackages&r can be held on &5Trains&r with &eDepots&r! Obviously the &eDepot&r needs to be connected to the &5Train &fvia &aGlue&r. \\n\\nNext, we can assign the &5Postbox&r to a &5Train Station&r by Right Clicking the &5Train Station&r wtih the &5Postbox&r in Hand. \\n\\nWe can then place the &5Postbox&r nearby and when a &5Train &farrives at the &5Station&r they will interact with the &5Postbox&r. \\n\\nIn the &5Postbox's&r GUI we can change its Address, which will effect whether &ePackages&r are delivered or sent from it. If the Address of the &ePackage&r matches the Address of the &5Postbox&r, it will be sent to the &5Postbox&r. If it doesn't match, it will go from the &5Postbox&r to your &5Train&r!"]
	quest.57A18F2E51952EB8.title: "&5Postboxes"
	quest.57A7A5C79389A96A.quest_desc: [
		"Most players already know Create, and yeah, all billion of its addons too. Not a lot of mods out there get whole damn modpacks built just for them, right?"
		""
		"If Create is new to you, no stress—these quests will get you sorted. Oh, and heads up: a ton of the items and machines have a Ponder option. Just hold W while you're hovering over an item to watch a little blueprint show you exactly how it works. Super handy."
		""
		"Seriously though, give Create a real shot. It's crazy useful once it clicks."
		""
		"First thing's first though: go find some Andesite. Like, a lot of it. You're gonna need it."
	]
	quest.57A7A5C79389A96A.title: "Create"
	quest.57B9DAA2ACB959B0.quest_desc: [
		"The Cutting Board is where you break down items into smaller pieces."
		""
		"How to: Place an item on the board (off-hand works best) and use a tool."
		"Tools matter: Use Knives for food, Axes for wood bark, and Pickaxes for bricks."
	]
	quest.584C7C381790301F.quest_desc: [
		"Now, you need to transform the oil to fuel. This is possible because of the Fuel Rafinery Block."
		""
		"If Oil is present in the first tank and if the block is powered, the oil will be transfered into Fuel and Diesel."
		""
		"The Fuel Rafinery block need to be powered."
	]
	quest.5876F5DE18D2FF80.quest_desc: [
		"Yeah, I'm not writing all that again."
		""
		"[ \"Check the \", { \"text\": \"Temperature\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"481311E0030FA4D3\" } }, \" chapter. You'll figure it out.\" ]"
	]
	quest.58819CE09A648A43.quest_subtitle: "These will be used to make most machines"
	quest.58819CE09A648A43.title: "Basic Building Components"
	quest.5932B5AD48F6AB74.quest_desc: ["Use power with a &5Pipe Booster&r to boost extraction speed of &2Oritech&r pipes."]
	quest.5932B5AD48F6AB74.quest_subtitle: "Makes them faster"
	quest.5979DE0E2BA3DAE5.quest_desc: ["&7Train Tracks&r are... well what you'll use to move &5Trains&r! \\n\\nYou'll need to &6Deploy&r 2 &7Iron Nuggets&r onto a &8Stone Slab&r, then &6Press&r it with a &6Metal Press&r to get 1. \\n\\nThese will be the first Block you place in order to get &5Trains&r as it will be needed to place &5Train Stations&r. \\n\\nThey have some limitations though, they can't go at steep angles to turn, or elevate. You'll need 4 Blocks of space to get up a Block with &7Train Tracks&r. To turn it is even worse! Let's just say, if you want a perfect circle with &7Train Tracks&r, it'll need a diameter of 18 Blocks."]
	quest.5979DE0E2BA3DAE5.title: "&7Train Tracks"
	quest.599B143AA8435D53.quest_desc: [
		"Winter blizzards are dangerous, but explosions are worse. If you want your loot to be 100% safe, you need the Obsidian Chest."
		"It’s as big as a Diamond Chest, but it’s completely blast-resistant. Not even a Creeper or a stray TNT can destroy your hard-earned supplies in this icy wasteland."
	]
	quest.5A352798AEE35D47.quest_desc: [
		"Skin it Off!"
		""
		"Now that the blood’s drained, you need to get through that hide. Grab a Skinning Knife to peel back the skin and reach the good stuff."
	]
	quest.5A352798AEE35D47.title: "Knives"
	quest.5B36DE3826F26963.quest_desc: ["&dRotational Power&r is the most important and confusing part of &6&lCreate&r. \\n\\nAll Machines will need some sort of &dRotational Power&r to work, but what is it and how do we use it? \\n\\n&dRotational Power&r is simply our Machines moving. Blocks like Shafts and Cogs will move that &dRotational Power&r to our Machines. \\n\\nTalking about Shafts, that is our start to &dRotational Power&r. They can be placed in a straight line, next to each other. \\n\\nWhen one &8Shaft&r is moved, all &8Shafts&r connected to it (on the same axis) will move with it. \\n\\nCraft 2 &8Andesite Alloys&r to create 8 &8Shafts&r."]
	quest.5B36DE3826F26963.title: "&d&lRotational Power"
	quest.5B6129FCC5398270.quest_desc: [
		"Spawners are now a real nightmare!"
		"Forget easy raiding—these things are as tough as Obsidian and will literally fight back if you try to break them. They’ll smash any torches or lights you place nearby, so no more \"cheating\" with brightness. "
		"When they're about to break, they’ll start smoking and might even explode in your face. If you're desperate, you can \"heal\" them with an Iron Block to keep the farm going, but otherwise, expect a brutal fight!"
	]
	quest.5B6221F6B645BD9C.quest_desc: [
		"When placing the pumpjack, you wont be able to get the pumpjack drill ! Make sure to place in a good place"
		""
		"When powered, the pumpjack will drain the oil in the chunk. Then, you will be able to getback the oil in buckets !"
	]
	quest.5B879DB488F784F0.quest_desc: [
		"Crystal Hearts:"
		""
		"You can use a crystal heart to permanently increase your health by one heart, using this method you can adquire an extra health bar. You might find an already crystal heart in a structure or find Crystal Heart Fragments from breaking mob spawners or as loot inside of important structures to craft one Crystal Heart."
	]
	quest.5B879DB488F784F0.title: "Increae your Health"
	quest.5BB4129931A4F057.quest_desc: ["Quests = Coins. Coins = Gacha. Simple as that! Use your rewards to buy pulls in the shop and pray to the RNG gods. Luck is a legit skill in Wintercraft, and since some loot is super rare, you'll need plenty of it. Ready to test your luck?"]
	quest.5BB4129931A4F057.title: "Shop"
	quest.5BDBC2358A239E4A.quest_desc: [
		"Don't have enough space in your icy shelter? Try Barrels!"
		""
		"They work exactly like Iron Chests, offering the same amount of slots (Iron, Gold, Diamond, etc.). The best part? You can open them even if there’s a solid block directly above. "
	]
	quest.5BF5AC6A5CE14226.quest_desc: ["Ready to build a real kitchen? The Workbench is your main station for everything in this mod. It’s not just for making Pizza or Toast; it’s where you craft all the essential appliances, cool furniture, and Fridges to keep your food fresh."]
	quest.5D4319A31D97392B.quest_desc: [
		"This mod significantly increases survival difficulty and adds a layer of realism. You must constantly monitor your body temperature, thirst, and overall health."
		""
		"Temperature depends on your environment and directly affects both your hunger and your chances of staying alive. A new hydration system is also in place—fail to drink enough water, and you will quickly become dehydrated."
		""
		"Furthermore, damage is now much more realistic; every limb can be individually injured, each resulting in different debuffs. With changes to the health system—including extra hearts, broken hearts—the game is tougher and more complex than ever."
		""
		"In this chapter, you’ll learn how it all works... well, hopefully."
	]
	quest.5D51665E0E3BA991.quest_desc: [
		"Aquaculture add various mechanics that can boost your chances of catching something while your line is cast, for example, bait. You can use use bait to increase your chances of catching a fish."
		""
		"Bait includes:"
		""
		"Worms "
		"Minnow "
		"Leech "
		""
		"You can obtain Leeches and Minnows by fishing, and Worms in a worm farm."
		""
		"A worm farm is a block you can craft to obtain worms that can be used as bait for fishing."
		"You can use any of the same items that can be used in the composter."
	]
	quest.5D74171C5FB953CC.quest_desc: [
		"Quick lore drop. The sky is alive and it hates pretty much everything. That's all you need to know for now."
		""
		"But here's the thing: the lore in this pack is completely optional. It's just there for flavor. You can live here, build a cozy base, and ignore it entirely. Or you can chase the story wherever it leads. Your call."
		""
		"Want more details? Check the other quest chapters from the others mods."
		""
		"Right now? Your only job is to survive. Everything else comes later."
	]
	quest.5DC892BA79EB52EC.quest_desc: ["The &6Mixer&r can do quite a few different Recipes but all will need a &8Basin&r below it! \\n\\nWe can &6Mix&r, this combines &bLiquids&f and &eItems&f into new &eItems&r. Like Baking! \\n\\n&6Brewing&r can combine the right &bLiquids &fand &eItems&r to make Liquid Potions. These can then be scooped out into Empty Bottles to get Potions. You'll need Heat from a &cBlaze Burner&r to &6Brew&r though. \\n\\nLast is &6Automated Shapeless Crafting&r. To the normal Player this might be a confusing statement but trust me it ain't that bad. &6Shapeless Crafting&r is a Recipe that can be made with the ingrediants in any pattern. \\n\\nLike Dying Wool, the Dye and Wool can be anywhere in the Crafting Table. Or even Silent Gear parts and patterns!"]
	quest.5DC892BA79EB52EC.title: "&6Mechanical Mixer"
	quest.5DD6631F5996BA71.quest_desc: ["&9Water Wheels&r are simple automatic &dRotational Power&r generators. \\n\\nSimply place them down, and have &9Water&r run over them in a certain direction. If it flows over both sides, it won't move, and the direction the &9Water&r flows determines where the &9Water Wheel&r &dRotates&r to. \\n\\nThe normal &9Water Wheel&r is just 1 Block big and provides a bit of Speed but with minimal Stress Units. \\n\\nThe &9Large Water Wheel&r takes up 3x3 area and grants more Stress Units, just at a lower Speed. \\n\\nYou can use both together to get the same Stress Units and Speed!"]
	quest.5DD6631F5996BA71.title: "&9Water Wheels"
	quest.5DEC826F3030D0EA.quest_desc: [
		"The forbidden item. This little thing is your ticket into the Nether."
		""
		"But heads up—the sky really doesn't like this one. When you craft it, you're gonna take some damage. Nothing crazy. Just a \"little\" reminder that you're breaking the rules."
		""
		"Don't say I didn't warn you."
	]
	quest.5E1404EF6D987991.quest_desc: [
		"Got the animal skins? Time to turn them into Leather."
		""
		"Place the skin on a Skin Rack (Right-click)."
		""
		"Add Salt (Right-click the skin)."
		""
		"Wet it down using a Wet Sponge, Rag."
		""
		"Now just wait for it to cure. It’s a bit of a process, but way better than just punchin' cows!"
	]
	quest.5E9AF8BB2C67DCCE.quest_subtitle: "Many ways to transport liquids"
	quest.5E9AF8BB2C67DCCE.title: "Transporting liquids"
	quest.5F29A45455127301.quest_desc: [
		"Cooling Coats will grant you resitance to Heat, making it easier to witstand the heat of hot biomes or NETHER."
		""
		"Common Cooling Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Heat Resistance by 2.0"
		""
		"Rare Cooling Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Heat Resistance by 3.0"
		""
		"Epic Cooling Coat:"
		""
		"Increases  Heat Resistance by 4.0"
	]
	quest.5F8363EC8F4499B6.quest_subtitle: "Making alloys"
	quest.5FA19C46F3C54F60.quest_desc: [
		"And then, there is the &lTrauma&r."
		""
		"Every time you fall and return to this frozen world, your soul carries a scar. You will see a single &lTrauma&r icon in your status, but do not be fooled. Underneath that icon, your body is failing in hidden ways. You may find yourself slower, weaker, or plagued by hunger and blindness."
		""
		"If you die again while the Trauma is still active, the symptoms will &lstack and worsen&r. What starts as a simple limp (Level I) can quickly escalate into a total physical collapse (Level IV) as more hidden ailments take hold."
		""
		"The only cure is &lsurvival&r. If you manage to stay alive until the Trauma fades, your next death will reset to Level I. But if you keep throwing your life away while traumatized, the winter will eventually break you for good."
	]
	quest.5FA19C46F3C54F60.title: "Trauma"
	quest.5FB58FA2EBFEDAEF.quest_desc: ["Runs on.. yeah, you know. Not gonna spell it out for you"]
	quest.602AA146EE1D6B3F.quest_desc: [
		"Got your Fire Starter or Flint and Steel? Nice. Now throw something flammable on that campfire. Wood, logs, sticks, whatever burns."
		""
		"Light it up and boom—you're officially not freezing to death anymore."
		""
		"You can now survive a few blocks away from the fire without turning into a popsicle. Progress."
		""
		"Congrats. You've unlocked the ability to exist. :)"
	]
	quest.611585852437E9AB.quest_desc: [
		"Wait, why is lapis here? Shouldn't this be later?"
		""
		"Nope. You can actually mine this stuff with a stone pickaxe. Weird flex, but okay."
		""
		"Grab some. You'll need it for enchanting later. Or just stare at the pretty blue color. Your choice."
	]
	quest.6134991F25B25B42.quest_desc: ["&lAssemblers&r not only allow you to craft &anewer items&r but also improve yield for some other items."]
	quest.6134991F25B25B42.quest_subtitle: "More than a crafter"
	quest.6134991F25B25B42.title: "Putting things together"
	quest.61377407192624DA.quest_desc: [
		"Alright, if you want better heating, better tools, or literally anything that doesn't suck, you're gonna need iron."
		""
		"Iron furnace? Needs iron. Most decent machines? Iron. Half the stuff you'll want later? You guessed it."
	]
	quest.613A84E4CFD30C72.quest_desc: [
		"Old Eye - Found in Desert Pyramids"
		""
		"Legends say this eye once belonged to one of the great Sandworms"
	]
	quest.617FECA8F759202A.quest_desc: [
		"Heads up... there are no graves in this world. When you die, your items drop just like in the old days. But that’s not even the worst part."
		""
		"The worst part? The mobs WILL pick up your armor and tools. They’re just doing what they must to survive the cold, even if it means looting your corpse. Good luck getting your gear back from a skeleton wearing your full enchanted set."
	]
	quest.617FECA8F759202A.title: "Death is just the beginning"
	quest.61D72A20301E5CED.quest_desc: [
		"Helmet: the wearer sees better underwater."
		"Chestpiece: the wearer breathes underwater."
		"Leggings: the wearer \"falls\" underwater."
		"Boots: the wearer swims faster."
	]
	quest.620D5C2FDE84604C.quest_desc: [
		"You wanna move fluids around? You're gonna need pipes. Simple as that."
		""
		"There's a few different types in the pack. Just make whatever feels right for you. They all do the same thing in the end—get liquid from point A to point B."
		""
		"Pick your favorite and craft some up."
	]
	quest.62353CED6FAA6B30.quest_desc: ["Because of the eternal winter, Hay Bales have frozen solid and don't provide as much as they used to. But hey, it's better than nothing. Find and smelt a Frozen Hay Bale in a furnace to make it usable again."]
	quest.6353A39CBEE599A0.quest_desc: ["You like combining Inventories and making a way of viewing and interacting with all those Inventories with a few simple &6Machines&r similar to &b&lAE2&r and &7&lSophisticated Storage&r? \\n\\nThen, you'll need some &eStock Links&r! \\n\\n&eStock Links&r can be placed on &ePackagers&r to connect to the Inventory the &ePackager&r is connected to. When first placed, a new &eStock Network&r will be created. \\n\\nThese can connect to Chests, Barrels, and even &eVaults&r! \\n\\nYou can also Right Click another &eStock Link&r with a &eStock Link&r in hand to tune them to the same &eNetwork&r. When the new &eStock Link&r is placed onto another &ePackager&r, its Inventory Block will be added to the same &eNetwork&r. \\n\\nIf you'd like to Interact with these &eNetworks&r you'll need other Blocks!"]
	quest.6353A39CBEE599A0.title: "&eStock Link"
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.quest_desc: ["&eTable Cloths&r can either be used to show off &eItems&r, or to sell off &eItems&r! \\n\\nTo set up a Shop, do all the steps from the previous Quest: placing &eStock Links&f, &eStock Tickers&r, and a Mob on a Seat or &cBlaze Burner&r. \\n\\nNow use a &eTable Cloth&r to Interact with the Mob or &cBlaze Burner&r, this will bind the &eTable Cloth&r to that &eStock Ticker&r. \\n\\nPlace down the &eTable Cloth&r and you'll be able to place the &eItems&r you want to sell on top, and the price below. \\n\\nWhen someone buys an &eItem&r, it will send a message to the &eStock Link&r, which will &ePackage&f the &eItems&r bought and take the price."]
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.quest_subtitle: "With Table Cloths"
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.title: "Shops"
	quest.64FF7118E29931C0.quest_desc: ["Before we get into the many &eItems&r we can get from the &6Millstone&r, let's talk about how to use it! \\n\\nFirst, it will need some &dRotational Power&r, don't worry it only needs a little. \\n\\nThen, you'll need to Drop the &eItem&r you want &6Milled&r, into the top of the &6Millstone&r. After it gets &6Milled&r, just Right Click the &6Millstone&r to take out your &eItems&r. \\n\\nNow, what &eItems&r can we get from the &6Millstone&r? We can get Dyes from pretty much every Flower, we can crush &7Stone&r into Gravel or other &7Stone&r like Blocks into similar Gravel Items. You can even get Wheat Flour from Wheat!"]
	quest.64FF7118E29931C0.title: "&6Millstone"
	quest.6539582429A70EE8.quest_subtitle: "Oritech can use power generated by most sources in this pack"
	quest.661B79FD805C3D3B.quest_desc: [
		"Want to pimp your rocket or explore planets even farther ? It's possible with Rocket Upgrade !"
		""
		"There are four type of Rocket Upgrades :"
		""
		"Motor Upgrade : This upgrade change the fuel needed by the Rocket"
		"Tank upgrade : This upgrade change the maximum capacity of the Rocket fuel tank"
		"Model Upgrade : This upgrade change the model of the rocket"
		"Skin Upgrade : This upgrade change the skin of the rocket"
		""
		"To applied theses upgrade, enter the rocket, open your inventory and place the upgrade in the good slot (It's one of the four slots at the bottom)"
	]
	quest.66F5E9BB705C458D.quest_desc: [
		"Think you're a pro? Prove it. In this frozen wasteland, every slot counts—but sometimes, you only get one."
		"This is the Dirt Chest 9000. It has exactly one slot. Use it wisely, or just keep it as a trophy of your struggles in the snow."
	]
	quest.672F9CF5B0E626F1.quest_desc: ["&ePackagers&r are the new and very important &6Machine&r for &6&lCreate&r. In order to use pretty much everything from the Update we'll need a &ePackager&r. \\nCombine some of our new-found &eCardboard&r to make a Block of Cardboard. No, these aren't &eBoxes&r yet and they certainly don't do anything. \\n\\nWell besides Crafting our &ePackager&r! The &ePackager&r will then be placed onto a Block with an Inventory, like Chest or Barrel. You'll know it is connected when one of the sides changes to appear like a wall. \\n\\nThen, when given a &4Redstone Signal&r it will pull all &eItems&r within the Inventory into a &ePackage&r! More on that later! \\n\\nThe &ePackages&r can then be pulled out by Hand or &eBelt&r. You can also send &ePackages&r back into the &ePackager&r to put the &eItems&r back into an Inventory. \\n\\nIf you place and name a Sign on the &ePackager&r it will give all &ePackages&r that it makes an Address."]
	quest.672F9CF5B0E626F1.title: "&ePackagers"
	quest.67431886C2D8BCE2.quest_desc: [
		"The Art of Butchery"
		""
		"Forget the old \"hit it till it drops\" routine. In this frozen wasteland, you can’t afford to be messy. Butchery makes hunting way more immersive (and rewarding!)."
		""
		"Grab a Butcher's Knife to finish off your prey. Instead of a few random items, you’ll get the whole corpse (sheep still drop their wool too, don't worry). From there, the real work begins!"
		""
		"Processing these carcasses gives you tons of high-protein food, which is a lifesaver in the cold. Just remember: while protein is king, you'll need more than just steak to stay healthy out there!"
	]
	quest.67431886C2D8BCE2.title: "The Art of Butchery"
	quest.67772BE65E0C232A.quest_desc: ["Greatly increases Experience gained from fishing, and if Quality Food is installed(it is), increases the Quality of caught fish!"]
	quest.67A46ED73E488CEE.quest_desc: ["&dGearshifts&r work similar to a &dClutch&r by connecting to our Systems and being powered by &4Redstone&r. \\n\\nInstead of stopping &dRotational Power&r though, the &dGearshift&r will change its Direction! \\n\\nIf it is going &e&oClockwise&r into the powered &dGearshift&r, it will come out &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r, and vice versa."]
	quest.67A46ED73E488CEE.title: "&dGearshift"
	quest.67C320FB510C28C4.quest_desc: [
		"Exotic Eye - Craft it using aquatic items"
		""
		"Those who followed this eye were never seen again; rumors say they found the great city of Atlantis, or lost their way trying"
	]
	quest.67D14F04EC8BAE2C.quest_desc: [
		"Want to go to space and explore new planets ? Well you first need a rocket!"
		""
		"First, you will need to craft the Rocket Station."
		""
		"Then, you will be able to craft the Rocket."
		""
		"There is only one recipe for the Rocket. You will be able to modify it with upgrades"
	]
	quest.67EEC2B0EB4D2E2F.quest_desc: ["This chapter is all about decorating your base, and while I only listed a few items here, you can find way more in JEI – but hey, it’s a start!"]
	quest.6893D537716AA748.quest_desc: ["&dCogwheels&r (&dCogs&r) are the next Block needed to use &dRotational Power&r! They can connect to &8Shafts&r or other &dCogs&r to move the &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThere is two versions of &dCogs&r: regular &dCogs &fand &dLarge Cogs&r. They will both act the same in the sense of &dRotational Power&r but there is also a few changes! \\nRegular &dCogs&r can connect to other &dCogs&r adjacent to them. This will move the &dRotational Power&r into a whole different direction. When this happens the direction of the second &dCog&r will be reversed. If the first &dCog&r is rotating &e&oClockwise&r, the second one will rotate &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\n&dLarge Cogs&r are a little more difficult to use than &dCogs&r. They can't connect to other &dLarge Cogs&r adjacent, rather they can only connect to &dCogs&r that are diagonal to them! \\n\\nMost &6Machines&r will need &dRotational Power&r from connecting &dCogs&r. You'll recognize if the &6Machine&r has an internal &dCog&r, that is what must be moved in order to use the &6Machine&r. "]
	quest.6893D537716AA748.quest_subtitle: "I just call them Cogs"
	quest.6893D537716AA748.title: "&dCogwheels&r!"
	quest.68B2AF27D01F7720.quest_desc: [
		"Now your choice begins. Which planet will you fly to? What awaits you there? You must experience it yourself."
		""
		"To start your rocket, you need to input some fuel in the left top slot. Then, when the Fuel Tank is full, just press the space bar."
	]
	quest.69642D475D36E491.quest_desc: [
		"Inventory space is a luxury in the cold! The Lunch Box is a lifesaver—it has 6 slots for food, but only takes up one slot in your inventory."
		""
		"You can eat directly from it, making it the perfect way to carry a full course meal without cluttering your pockets. Keep your proteins, veggies, and fruits all in one handy box!"
	]
	quest.69796E3DE6694D92.quest_desc: [
		"Windmills are a bit more fiddly than Water Wheels, but you get way more customization. And of course, better Speed and Stress Units to play with."
		""
		"First up, you need the heart of the whole thing: the Windmill Bearing. This block is where the Rotational Power comes out, and it's also what you'll use to actually turn the Windmill on."
		""
		"Next, you need blocks to build the actual sail part. Blocks will automatically stick to the Bearing itself, but for the rest of the structure? You'll need Glue. Only exception is Windmill Sails—those attach on their own, no glue required."
		""
		"You'll want at least 8 sail-like blocks. That means either actual Windmill Sails or just plain Wool. The more you slap on there, the faster the whole thing spins."
		""
		"Once it's all built, just Right Click the Bearing with an empty hand to fire it up."
	]
	quest.69E79B0592DE0701.quest_desc: [
		"The Gold Fern is a rare drop that exist in the Gold Sun Fern Leaf and the Gold Ice Fern Leaf variants, you can use it to craft potions of heat inmunity (Gold Ice Fern Leaf) and cold inmunity (Gold Hot Fern Leaf)."
		""
		"These potions are not needed to visit the Nether or the End."
		""
		"There is a 1/100 chances of a Ice Fern Bush or a Sun Fern Bush to, when fully grown suddenly turn golden. You can also naturally find them in the wilderness."
	]
	quest.69EE22CB4FF1E591.quest_desc: [
		"Contraptions can feel a little brain-melty at first, but here's the simple version: it's just the art of sticking a bunch of blocks and machines together so they all move as one big system."
		""
		"You'll need a few things. Something to actually make it move, like a Linear Chassis. Whatever machines you want doing work on it, like Drills. And of course, Glue to hold the whole mess together."
		""
		"Once it's all glued up and you feed some Rotational Power to the moving part, the whole contraption should come alive and do its thing."
	]
	quest.69EE22CB4FF1E591.title: "Contraptions"
	quest.69FB4EC4261467FE.quest_desc: [
		"Functional Drawers is a storage mod that provides an easy solution to storing tons of items in a single block. "
		""
		"Drawers come in three varieties which are Single Drawers, 1x2 Drawers, and 2x2 Drawers. While a 2x2 drawer can store four separate items the total base storage amount is also divided by four. "
		"To place an item in simply right click on the Drawer with the item. "
		"Double right clicking will deposit multiple stacks at a time. "
		"To remove items from a Drawer left clicking it will remove one item at a time while sneak and left clicking will pull out a full stack."
	]
	quest.6A592440FEC22F09.quest_desc: ["normal arrows fired from it are not impeded underwater."]
	quest.6A6EEC9C9E52AE13.quest_desc: [
		"Congrats. You made it to the Nether."
		""
		"It's like 35+ degrees Celsius in here. Maybe more. I don't know how you're gonna survive this heat, but hey, that's your problem now."
	]
	quest.6A7018604D129454.quest_desc: ["cauldron that allows you to add a persistent enchantment to an item by throwing the item in it after having filled it with a stack of lapis lazuli"]
	quest.6A7932669B151A7B.quest_desc: [
		"Eighty percent dirt. Two percent diamond or netherite scrap. You see these odds?"
		""
		"Yes. You read that correctly. You will mostly get dirt. So much dirt. Mountains of dirt. Your grandchildren will inherit dirt."
		""
		"But that two percent... that two percent is why you're standing here, staring at a chest made of compressed disappointment, hoping today is your lucky day."
		""
		"Spoiler: it's probably not. But you're going to open it anyway. Because what if?"
		""
		"\"80% disappointment. 2% glory. 100% gambling addiction.\""
	]
	quest.6A7932669B151A7B.title: "80% dirt"
	quest.6B95B552B03A919C.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the Kitchen!"
		""
		"Survival in the eternal winter isn't just about not freezing—it's about what you eat. While meat gives you those essential proteins, you won't last long without vegetables and fruits. A balanced diet is the only way to keep your body running in this frost!"
		""
		"Before we start cooking gourmet meals, we need a heat source. You have a few ways to start:"
		""
		"Campfire: The absolute basic. It’s cheap, provides light, and works in a pinch, but it's not the most efficient for a real chef."
		""
		"Primitive Stove: A solid middle ground. You can craft it early, but you'll need to keep feeding it fuel to keep the flames alive."
		""
		"Stove: The ultimate upgrade. It’s pricier, but it burns forever without any fuel. It’s the \"gold standard\" for any serious base."
		""
		"Pick your flame and let’s get cooking!"
	]
	quest.6D04FB7ECBB977DA.quest_desc: [
		"To create oxygen, you first need to craft the water separator. This machines separate oxygen and the hydrogen from the water."
		""
		"The Water Separator need to be powered!"
	]
	quest.6D8597912E0804E1.quest_desc: [
		"As you’ve already noticed, it’s winter... This means crops can normally only be planted during specific seasons. Since it's an eternal winter, farming outside is impossible."
		""
		"However, there is a way: Greenhouses. If your crops have light, water, and glass blocks above them, they will grow normally. Just keep in mind—it won't be fast."
	]
	quest.6D8597912E0804E1.title: "Crops"
	quest.6D8672CBDAE6E542.quest_desc: ["You can use the Fish Display to show off your best catches, so instead of just eating everything, you can hang your favorite fish on the wall and flex your fishing skills to anyone who visits your frozen base!"]
	quest.6D99195811DC60B6.quest_desc: ["???????????"]
	quest.6DE192E5462ACBDC.quest_desc: [
		"This thing lets you enchant items way past the normal level 30 cap. We're talking up to level 64. No limits, just pure power."
		""
		"But keep in mind—push your luck too hard and you might slap a curse on that shiny sword of yours. The sky has a sense of humor, apparently."
		""
		"Also, heads up: you'll need to put lapis in the slots next to the item. Twice as much as a normal enchanting table. Yeah, it's hungry. Feed it blue rocks or get nothing."
	]
	quest.6E105445D7BC2B5C.quest_desc: ["The classic. With this bad boy, you can finally mine diamonds , gold and redstone."]
	quest.6E11173966DD5565.quest_desc: [
		"Artifacts is a mod designed to make exploration truly rewarding by adding powerful items that cannot be crafted."
		""
		"You can find these treasures in vanilla structures, through archaeology, or very rarely worn by enemies. If you're wondering what a specific item does, don't worry—the effect of each artifact is clearly described in its tooltip."
		""
		"A word of warning for this modpack: In &bEternal Winter&r, these artifacts are significantly rarer than usual. Finding one is a true stroke of luck and a testament to your survival skills."
		""
		"Keep an eye out for Underground Campsites. While they contain loot, some chests are actually Mimics—dangerous monsters that attack if you get too close. However, the risk is worth it: a killed Mimic is guaranteed to drop a random artifact."
	]
	quest.6E11173966DD5565.title: "Artifacts"
	quest.6E70417877AFC539.quest_desc: [
		"At this point, you should honestly start a YouTube series. \"1000 Ways to Die in WinterCraft\" would be a hit. You've already got most of the footage."
		""
		"Your ghost has seen more of this world than your living body. That's not an achievement. That's a lifestyle."
		""
		"Some players build bases. You build experience. The hard way. Repeatedly."
	]
	quest.6E70417877AFC539.quest_subtitle: "come back when you die this many times"
	quest.6E70417877AFC539.title: "75"
	quest.6E7925E26F9A47BE.quest_desc: ["do not have a mining speed penalty when underwater."]
	quest.6EA96E6CC23CF2C0.quest_desc: [
		"Aquaculture add a new material called Neptunium to the game. You can make tools and armor from Neptunium or Neptunium from Stellaris mod, but let's be real—fishing is way faster than building a whole rocket just to fly to another planet :). This material has various properties when underwater."
		""
		"You can obtain this equipment, or Neptunium Ingots to craft it yourself, by getting it from Neptune's Bounty. Neptune's Bounty is rare treasure loot. (Luck of the Sea enchantment increases the chance of getting Neptune's Bounty)or even find it on Venus  "
	]
	quest.6EAABA968E659953.quest_desc: ["Keeps fish from escaping when collecting Treasure Chests, and increases the chances that Treasures will appear!"]
	quest.6EBFA16D212A7B22.quest_subtitle: "Betterest"
	quest.6EEB2BFEA8A89220.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6F0A636B6CFCAB36.quest_desc: [
		"Runs on biomass."
		""
		"Make biomass to use it"
	]
	quest.6F0A76CC8E496BC2.quest_desc: [
		"Look, it’s not just about your overall HP anymore. Depending on how you get smacked, one of your limbs is gonna take the hit. Think of each limb as a chunk of your total health—if you lose one, your max HP bar shrinks."
		"If a limb gets trashed or completely snaps, you’re in for some nasty debuffs depending on what’s broken. Sure, you can technically survive with every single limb broken, but honestly? Your chances of staying alive at that point are basically zero. Keep 'em intact if you don't want to crawl your way through the snow!"
	]
	quest.6F2B86E609C99877.quest_desc: ["Met a Golem you didn't like? Regular blades will just blunt against metal or stone. For the toughest \"mobs\" like Iron Golems, you’ll need a Hacksaw. Use it just like a Cleaver to take them apart piece by piece."]
	quest.6F420A3A8AD4894F.quest_desc: [
		"Before we even think about launching into space, we're gonna need some steel. Like, a lot of it."
		""
		"There's three different types of steel in this pack. Pick whichever one feels easiest for you. Doesn't really matter which—they all get the job done."
		""
		"Just get your hands on some and we'll go from there."
	]
	quest.6F420A3A8AD4894F.title: "Steel"
	quest.6F779C8ED4781B66.quest_desc: [
		"One. Hundred. Deaths."
		""
		"You magnificent disaster. You beautiful train wreck. You absolute legend of failure."
		""
		"Most players would have uninstalled. You doubled down. You tripped. You fell. You got back up. One hundred times."
		""
		"The frost has stopped trying to kill you. It's now just curious how many ways you can find to die next. The bedbugs have unionized and demanded hazard pay. Nightmares tell stories about YOU now."
		""
		"This isn't a skill issue anymore. This is a commitment issue. And you are committed."
	]
	quest.6F779C8ED4781B66.quest_subtitle: "come back when you die this many times"
	quest.6F779C8ED4781B66.title: "100"
	quest.6FB8EBEE24BF5D2E.quest_desc: ["Using Ice Ferns or Sun Ferns you can craft special strings that you can use to craft and apply coats on your armors using a sew  table."]
	quest.6FCED39795475662.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations. You have died ten times."
		""
		"The pack was tested. It was beaten. The developer survived. So can you."
		""
		"This is not a bug. This is not bad luck. This is a skill issue. And skill can be improved."
		""
		"Take a moment. Breathe. Think about what went wrong. Was it the eternal winter? The nightmares?"
		"Or did you just walk off a cliff while reading quest descriptions?"
		""
		"Whatever it was, learn from it. Adapt. Overcome. The next ten deaths will be more educational."
		""
		"Or not. We'll be here counting."
	]
	quest.6FCED39795475662.quest_subtitle: "come back when you die this many times"
	quest.6FCED39795475662.title: "10"
	quest.6FFD0301AC8C83ED.quest_subtitle: "Using less energy"
	quest.7032AC2B9066CC39.quest_desc: ["Place it on an addon slot and you will get more space to place your addons."]
	quest.7032AC2B9066CC39.quest_subtitle: "More addons!"
	quest.7084E47579D62B52.quest_subtitle: "A circuit to do more"
	quest.70AD105E7A3248CE.quest_desc: [
		"This thing lets you bump up every enchant on an item by one level. Cost? 32 echo shards per upgrade."
		""
		"You can push it all the way to level 74, but once you hit a certain point—some roman numeral nonsense—you'll need a Nether Star per level to keep going."
		""
		"Too overpowered? Yeah, probably. But hey, there's gotta be something broken in the pack, right? If you love the grind, this is your endgame."
		""
		"Oh, and to make your life slightly less painful, there's a recipe for echo shards: one Sculk Shrieker gives you 16 shards. You're welcome."
	]
	quest.70B5311BDB9C20B5.quest_desc: [
		"Torches. They give light. That's about it."
		""
		"Don't get too comfortable though. After a while, they burn out and die on you. And no, standing next to one won't keep you warm. Don't even try."
		""
		"They're fine for the very beginning. Helps you see. But long term? You're gonna want something better."
		""
		"Invest in real lighting later. For now, this'll do."
	]
	quest.70FAD4013FA8A14A.quest_subtitle: "Increase the processing speed"
	quest.716259D8E16F1979.quest_desc: [
		"Wanna make that fishing minigame a piece of cake? "
		"Get yourself some Bobbers. They add special buffs to your rod and are super easy to use."
		""
		"How to equip: "
		"Forget about fancy tables! Just grab a Bobber in your inventory, drag it over your fishing rod, and right-click. Boom, it's equipped!"
		""
		"What they do: Different bobbers give different perks. Some make the \"fishing bar\" bigger, some slow down escaping fish, and others even help you find rare treasure chests."
		""
		"It's the fastest way to stop struggling and start catching the big ones. Try out different types and see which one fits your style!"
	]
	quest.716259D8E16F1979.title: "Bobbers"
	quest.717029801B7E34EE.quest_desc: [
		"The Gold Fern is a rare drop that exist in the Gold Sun Fern Leaf and the Gold Ice Fern Leaf variants, you can use it to craft potions of heat inmunity (Gold Ice Fern Leaf) and cold inmunity (Gold Hot Fern Leaf)."
		""
		"There is a 1/100 chances of a Ice Fern Bush or a Sun Fern Bush to, when fully grown suddenly turn golden. You can also naturally find them in the wilderness."
	]
	quest.71B1B53A03A16296.quest_desc: ["&bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r are used with &aContraptions&r that are using &bFluid Tanks&r. \\n\\nIn order to access the &bFluid Tanks&r you'll need two &bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r, one connected to the &aContraption&r and one connected to &bFluid Pipes&r. \\n\\nThe &bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r will need a 1 or 2 Block gap between a meeting point in order for them to work. \\n\\nIf we have all that, the &bPortable Fluid Interface&r connected to the &aContraption&r will stop the &aContraption&r to either take &bFluids&r in or out from the second &bPortable Fluid Interface&r to add it to the &bFluid Tanks&r within the &aContraption&r."]
	quest.71B1B53A03A16296.title: "&bPortable Fluid Interfaces"
	quest.72C094368F2F0FF4.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't noticed yet, there's no minimap or coordinates in this pack. Your only option is this Atlas."
		""
		"It shows your coordinates and gives you a decent map of where you are. Vanilla style, nothing fancy."
		""
		"Better learn to use it, or get used to being lost forever."
	]
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.quest_desc: ["The &dHand Crank&r is the simplest and worst form of &dRotational Power&r generation. \\n\\nWhen you hold Right Click it'll move &e&oClockwise&r and if you hold Shift Right Click it will move &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\nIt only gives a tiny bit of Stress Units and will stop after you quit holding it."]
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.quest_subtitle: "Manual Power!"
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.title: "&dHand Crank"
	quest.72E7AE66F2A7C4C4.quest_subtitle: "Use fluid in machines"
	quest.73CDED178832C767.quest_desc: [
		"[ \"As you’ve already noticed... or maybe not. You must keep a close eye on your body temperature, hydration, and make sure you don't injure your limbs. You can find more detailed information in this \", { \"text\": \"CHAPTER\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"5D4319A31D97392B\" } }, \".\" ]"
		"Additionally, when you first spawn into this world, you have about 5 minutes to prepare—that’s how long the Temperature Immunity effect lasts. It gives you some breathing room before the cold starts to bite. You’ll get the same effect after you die, but only for 3 minutes."
	]
	quest.73CDED178832C767.title: "Temperature/Thirst/Health"
	quest.743F7B8F9E7728C0.quest_desc: ["chance to not use durability"]
	quest.7455343995D2C714.quest_desc: ["Dropped from Ancient Knights. Used for upgrade orbs"]
	quest.748829C71CDF5E69.quest_desc: ["Runs on furnace fuel"]
	quest.74BF2368D12E6836.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the world of &bEternal Winter&r. You will find many altered mechanics here, specifically designed to make your survival much more challenging. These quests are here to guide you through the basics and help you stay alive—though in the end, your success depends entirely on your own skills."
		""
		"I won’t be diving into every single mod or explaining everything in detail. That would be too easy and, frankly, quite boring. The true charm of this pack lies in discovering things for yourself."
		"So... will you survive? Will you reach the end? Or will you give up? The choice is yours."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"I said I wouldn’t dive into every single mod or explain everything in detail. I said that would be too easy and boring, and that the true charm lies in discovering things yourself."
		"Well... I might have lied a bit. Looking at the amount of quests I’ve made, I clearly couldn’t help myself! I’ve ended up diving pretty deep into these some mods to make sure you’re prepared."
		"But the question remains: Even with all this help, will you survive? Will you reach the end, or will the frost still take you?"
		"The choice is yours. Now get to work."
	]
	quest.74FA9E3BB7282E29.quest_desc: [
		"One of the most important thing for a living creature to live is Oxygen ! Without Oxygen, you die."
		""
		"Let's learn how to create oxygen "
	]
	quest.752C3CC713AC3709.quest_desc: ["Some targets are just too tough for a knife. If you’re dealing with Turtles or Shulkers, a Cleaver won't cut it. You need a Hammer to smash through those shells! Just right-click the carcass to crack it open and get the goods inside."]
	quest.754B8F1FBCD983C5.quest_desc: ["&eStock Tickers&r can be set to the &eNetwork&r by Right Clicking the &eStock Link &fwith the &eStock Ticker&r in Hand. \\n\\nThen, place down the &eStock Ticker&r and give it a &eStock Keeper&r by either placing down a &cBlaze Burner&r or a Mob on a Seat nearby. \\n\\nYou'll know they are a &eStock Keeper&r by their stereotypical &aGreen&r Visor. We can now Right Click the &eStock Keeper&r to view and order &eItems&r from our &eNetwork&r. \\n\\nWhen you order &eItems&r, they'll be placed into a &ePackage &ffrom a &ePackager &fbelow the &eStock Link&r."]
	quest.754B8F1FBCD983C5.title: "&eStock Ticker"
	quest.757825C801CDDA36.quest_desc: [
		"So, what is the optimal temperature?"
		""
		"In this modpack, the \"sweet spot\" is below 24°C. "
		"But be careful:"
		"Cold: At 8°C, Hypothermia will set in. "
		"Once you hit 2°C, you’ll start losing health rapidly."
		"Heat: At 30°C, you’ll suffer from Heatstroke, which turns into constant damage once you reach 35°C."
		""
		"Keep your thermometer close and stay within the safe range!"
	]
	quest.757825C801CDDA36.title: "Temperature States"
	quest.758FF838D9E15C09.title: "Chests"
	quest.769F835C0DB4976F.quest_desc: ["Need some salt for your recipes? It’s easy: just put a Bucket of Water on the Electric Stove. Wait a bit, and you've got yourself some salt. Simple as that!"]
	quest.76CBFA38D021AC95.quest_desc: ["&dWindmills&r are a little more complicated than &9Water Wheels&r, but they also come with more customization and of course Speed and Stress Units! \\n\\nFirst, you'll need the heart of the &dWindmill&r, the &dWindmill Bearing&r. This Block will send the &dRotational Power&r out of it. It is also what we'll use to turn on the &dWindmill&r! \\n\\nThen, you'll need the Blocks to make the actual &dWindmill&r part. Blocks will automatically stick to the &dBearing&r, but to the rest of the &dWindmill&r you'll need &aGlue&r. Besides &dWindmill Sails&r, those attach automatically! \\n\\nWe'll also need atleast 8 &dWindmill Sail&r like Blocks, those being the &dWindmill Sails&r or Wool. The more we have, the faster the &dWindmill&r spins! \\n\\nOnce it is all set, just Right Click the &dBearing&r with an Empty Hand to start it up."]
	quest.76CBFA38D021AC95.title: "&dWindmills"
	quest.76DE87D79DF58063.quest_desc: [
		"Farming in the tundra means you'll be carrying a lot of seeds, and they can quickly clutter up your pockets. The Seed Pouch is here to save your inventory space!"
		""
		"It allows you to store a massive amount of seeds—way more than a standard stack of 64. The only catch? It can only hold one type of seed at a time. It’s the perfect tool for a dedicated farmer planning a massive harvest."
	]
	quest.77382D4114E901CB.quest_desc: ["The &bHose Pulley&r is used to take and place full Source Blocks of &bFluids&r, yes not just &9Water&r. \\n\\nFirst, set how far the &bHose&r actually goes down or up with the &8Shaft&r at one side. Either with a &6Cog&f, &8Shaft&r, or &dHand Crank&r which is easiest. \\n\\nThen, on the other side of the &bHose Pulley&r we can put some &bFluid Pipes&r. With &bMechanical Pumps&r we can choose whether the &bHose Pulley&r picks up &bFluid&r Sources or place them down. \\n\\nThe &bHose Pulley&r only has an Inventory of 1.5 Buckets or 1500mB, but the &bFluids&r can be &bPiped&r into other Inventories or &bTanks&r! \\n\\nIf the &9Water&r Source is infinite, the &bHose Pulley&r won't take out Source Blocks, but will keep taking &bFluid&r out. \\n\\nThis will also work with &cLava&r Source Blocks, but those aren't infinite. So you might want to check out &c&lThe Nether&r for that as it is pretty much infinite there!"]
	quest.77382D4114E901CB.title: "&bHose Pulley"
	quest.77BE3D9D274F72F1.quest_desc: ["&5Train Stations&r are the most important Blocks for &5Trains&r! We need them for making &5Trains&f, breaking down &5Trains&r, and Scheduling them! \\n\\nTo use them, you'll need to select a &7Train Track&r with them. Hold the &5Train Station&r in your Hand and Right Click a &7Train Track&r. \\n\\nI don't know the max distance a &5Train Station&r can be placed, it is atleast 10 Blocks! (I don't have that much room to test). \\n\\nOnce placed you can Rename it with the Text Bar at the top. \\n\\nYou can also Click \"Create New Train\", to start making your first &5Train&r. After you Clicked it, one of the &7Tracks&r will appear &9Blue&r, this is the &7Track&r you can place &5Boogeys&r on. \\n\\nRight Click that &7Track&r with a &5Train Casing&r to make a &5Boogey&r, AKA &5Train Wheels&r. Right Click the actual Wheels to change its design. Then you can..."]
	quest.77BE3D9D274F72F1.title: "&5Train Stations"
	quest.77E1D4ABE3C1F62E.quest_desc: [
		"Temperature Modifier Effect:"
		"&#FF934AHot Food &r"
		"+1 Temperature &r"
		"Hot Food II"
