	quest.781417E81E290D2A.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.78656C89EEE80DB5.quest_desc: ["&eBrass Tunnels&r work like &eAndesite Tunnels&r just with so many more configurations! \\n\\nFirst, we now get Filters! These are per side: if you Filter the Input side, only that Filter &eItem&r will be allowed to move throught the &eTunnel&r. If you Filter the Output sides, then only those &eItems&r will come out of its side. \\n\\nNow we can also line &eBrass Tunnels&r together. This will allow them to take all the same Inputs but Filter them out to certain &eBelts&r! \\n\\nAt the top of the &eTunnel&r we'll find the option to change its Distribution Modes. I won't explain them in too much detail, our Quests have limited space, instead I'll summarize! \\n\\nSplit: will split the &eItem&r stacks evenly per how many &eBelts&r it will go to. Forced Split: will make sure every &eBelt&r will get an even amount, while normal Split might skip some. Round Robin: will alternate individually between each &eBelt&r. Forced Round Robin: won't skip some &eItems&r and instead will wait, everyone gets a turn! Prefer Nearest: will send the &eItems&r to the closest Output. Randomize: it sends the &eItems&r randomly to different Outputs. Synchronize Inputs: will only Output when every &eBrass Tunnel&r has an &eItem&r waiting to Input."]
	quest.78656C89EEE80DB5.title: "&eBrass Tunnel"
	quest.78D1947BA043B465.quest_desc: ["Runs on Coal"]
	quest.792751CD9A15A932.quest_desc: ["Listen up, in this frozen world, temperature is your biggest frenemy. You’ve gotta watch out so you don’t turn into a popsicle, but don't overdo it the other way either—overheating sucks just as much. If you get too chilly or way too hot, you’ll first catch some nasty debuffs, then your HP will slowly tank until you’re toast. Luckily, there are tons of modifiers and ways to keep your body temp in check."]
	quest.7937DE650CABC1FF.quest_subtitle: "Runs on furnace fuel"
	quest.7939325B771F0D29.quest_desc: [
		"Alright, this one's a doozy, so pay attention."
		""
		"First up, actually building the Steam Engine. The Fluid Tanks are what matters here—they decide how much Water you can hold, which sets the level your Steam Engine runs at."
		""
		"Slap the Steam Engine block onto the side of the Fluid Tanks and boom, you've got yourself a Steam Boiler. Then stick a Shaft on the Steam Engine to get that mechanical arm moving. That's where your Rotational Power comes out."
		""
		"Second, you need a Heat Source. Gotta put something hot under the Fluid Tanks to get that Water boiling. Plenty of options: Fire, Campfires, Lava, Magma Blocks. But honestly? Blaze Burners are the best, hands down."
		""
		"Better Heat Source means more Stress Units. Feed those Blaze Burners some Blaze Cakes and you'll be cruising."
		""
		"Third, Water. Obviously. No Water, no Steam. Pretty simple."
		""
		"How you pipe the Water in is up to you. Figure it out."
	]
	quest.7940E65759BE7CCF.quest_desc: [
		"Blocks all effect from wounder limbs"
		""
		"None"
	]
	quest.796129D93FFD13B8.quest_desc: [
		"If chasing animals in the snow isn't your thing, why not try the water? Fishing is a solid alternative to hunting, especially when you're stuck near a frozen lake. But don't expect it to be a chill \"AFK\" activity – it's a bit of a challenge now."
		""
		"What you need to know for now:"
		""
		"When you hook something, a Stardew Valley style bar pops up. Keep the green box on the fish to catch it. Miss it, and you’re going home hungry."
	]
	quest.796129D93FFD13B8.title: "Fishing"
	quest.79E8A53149824928.quest_desc: ["Upgrade time! I added this Electric Boiler because, well... someone had to. Forget the coal; just hook this up to your power supply and enjoy that sweet, constant heat. Power is the ultimate survival skill."]
	quest.7A31016B07968296.quest_desc: ["Runs on radioactive item like uranium ingot or block."]
	quest.7A999334A0001B20.quest_desc: [
		"Undead Eye - Craft it using an Undead Soul"
		""
		"Remembrance of the past lives of those who live in death"
	]
	quest.7ADE23CE1F32ADC5.quest_desc: ["The Scroll Forge is used to craft scrolls by using ink, paper, and a focus. The ink determines the rarity (and therefore level), and the focus determines spell’s school."]
	quest.7B84839FD330D40F.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.7C16991DCF2D9FFC.quest_desc: ["chance to not use durability and increased luck."]
	quest.7C69AFB7F80D89FF.quest_desc: [
		"Crying Obsidian. The purple stuff that looks like it's having a bad day."
		""
		"How do you get it? Few ways, your choice as always:"
		""
		"Find it in the world. Rare, but it spawns naturally in ruined portals and some structures."
		""
		"Use Create machines. Yeah, you can actually make this stuff if you know what you're doing."
		""
		"Alchemy cauldron. Toss some regular obsidian in with the right ingredients and watch it cry."
		""
		"Nether. Barter with piglins or find it in bastions."
		""
		"Pick whatever method doesn't make you want to cry along with it."
	]
	quest.7C8CDD259495A31A.quest_desc: ["&eTunnels&r at the most basic level, will cover your &eBelts&r. This will make it so the &eItems&r can't be picked up, and hopefully the Mobs won't leave. \\n\\nIf you place another &eBelt&r moving perpendicular to the &eBelt&r the &eTunnel&r is on, the &eTunnel&r will filter 1 &eItem&r from the Stack of &eItems&r to the perpendicular &eBelt&r, while leaving the rest of the &eItems&r on the first &eBelt&r. \\n\\nIf there is just 1 &eItem&r, it will move through the &eTunnel&r like normal."]
	quest.7C8CDD259495A31A.title: "&eAndesite Tunnel"
	quest.7CBAD1047B087803.quest_desc: [
		"Now you have the &eclumps&r, using a fluid addon on a centrifuge will allow you to input &aSulphuric Acid&r into it. When &eclumps&r are processed with this acid, you will get gems."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can use &9Water&r for a lower yield."
		""
		"&l&o&nNote&r"
		""
		"Currently, some recipes are broken which output dusts or nuggets."
	]
	quest.7CBAD1047B087803.quest_subtitle: "Centrifuging a clump gives me gems....?"
	quest.7CBAD1047B087803.title: "Spinning into gems"
	quest.7D2F41DD9774DDA7.title: "Transporting items"
	quest.7D67058592EE5958.quest_desc: [
		"The Cannon is the fun part. It actually builds the structure from the schematic for you. Just set up some chests nearby with all the blocks and materials it needs, and feed it some gunpowder for fuel."
		""
		"Boom. Literally. It'll blast that building into existence without you lifting a finger."
	]
	quest.7DA16B4D8BEA9E88.quest_desc: [
		"The Thermometer is the most important item in this world. Without it, you’ll never know if you're about to survive or freeze to death."
		"How does it work?"
		""
		"In Hand: "
		"While holding it, the needle shows real-time temperature changes. Right-click to check the exact temperature of your surroundings."
		""
		"Baubles Slot: "
		"You can wear it to constantly monitor your own body heat."
		""
		"Item Frame:"
		"Hang it on a wall to use it as a stationary indicator for your base."
	]
	quest.7EB11A9263D95746.quest_desc: [
		"The Hand Crank is the absolute simplest way to make Rotational Power. Also the worst. But hey, it's something."
		""
		"Hold Right Click and it spins Clockwise. Hold Shift + Right Click and it goes Counter-Clockwise."
		""
		"It barely gives you any Stress Units to work with, and the second you let go, it stops. Don't expect miracles from this thing."
	]
	quest.7EC8AB3631A9DC64.quest_desc: [
		"You actually did it. You’ve cooked your way through the entire cookbook while the rest of the world is out there freezing and eating raw berries. From simple broths to legendary feasts, you’ve mastered every recipe and turned this frozen wasteland into your personal kitchen."
		"You aren't just a survivor anymore—you are the Legendary Chef of the Eternal Winter. Your base probably smells better than any other place in this cursed world! Take this reward and keep the fires burning."
	]
	quest.7EC8AB3631A9DC64.title: "!CHEF!"
	quest.7EEEEDD5FF31ACD3.quest_desc: ["The &eSmart Chute&r is a &eChute&r with the options to Filter."]
	quest.7EEEEDD5FF31ACD3.title: "&eSmart Chute"
	quest.7F0F7111552F95A9.quest_desc: ["Okay we got our fully Assembled &5Train&r, now how do we use it? \\n\\nIf you are Controlling it, you'll need to Right Click the &5Train Controls&r. \\n\\nThen, you can Hold W to move Forward or Hold S to go Backwards. No, &5Trains&r don't turn like Cars do, they just follow the &7Tracks&r. \\n\\nGoing Forward you'll pick up a lot of Speed, you can see it in the Bar that replaces your &aExperience Bar&r. Backwards won't give as much Speed. \\n\\nIf you are getting near a &5Train Station&r and not moving at the speed of light, you can Hold Space to stop the &5Train&f at the &5Station&r. This is helpful for disassembling them or even connecting more &5Boogeys&r."]
	quest.7F0F7111552F95A9.title: "Controlling your &5Train"
	quest.7F48EE8F8A5852F5.quest_desc: ["But heads up—it needs power to actually work. You'll need a Power Bank to charge the thing up."]
	quest.7F5A877AD4DC6B2F.quest_desc: [
		"You can’t craft Rich Soil—you have to grow it. Place Organic Compost on the ground and let it decompose over time. It craves sunlight and moisture, but you can speed it up by placing \"activators\" like mushrooms, podzol, or other compost blocks in a 3x3 area around it."
		""
		"Why bother?"
		""
		"Growth Boost: It acts like a permanent bone meal for your plants."
		"Rich Farmland: Use a hoe to till it. It’s immune to mob trampling and won't break when melons or pumpkins grow!"
		""
		"Mushroom Colonies: Plant a mushroom in the dark to grow a massive colony."
		"Pro Tip: Keep an eye out for Compost Houses in Plains Villages. Villagers build these smelly Compost Heaps to process leftovers on a large scale—it’s a great way to find Rich Soil without the wait!"
	]
	quest.7F8E50FA436DB4E6.quest_desc: ["&dEncased Chain Drives&r will act similar to &eBelts&r, by connecting &8Shafts&r to each other in a row. \\n\\nThere is quite a few differences though, like that &dEncased Chain Drives&r can be used with a &6Wrench&r to rotate. They also need to be placed directly next to other &dChain Drives&r to keep &dRotating&r. \\n\\nLike &eBelts&r though, they keep the same Speed and Stress Units as the original &8Shaft&r. Plus they keep the same direction!"]
	quest.7F8E50FA436DB4E6.title: "&dEncased Chain Drives"
